<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Approve Product Offering for Launch/Rollout">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Approve Product Offering for Launch/Rollout</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Not used for this process element</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Assess Performance of Existing Product Offering -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Assess Performance of Existing Product Offering">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Assess Performance of Existing Product Offering</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Assess Performance of Existing Product Offering analyzes the performance of an existing product offering to identify inadequacies and required improvements. The process uses information from customers and from operational activities to identify required improvements.

Required improvements may involve those to a product specification upon which the offering is based. In this case the improvements are communicated to the Develop Detailed Product Specification process.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Manage Product Offering Exit -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Manage Product Offering Exit">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Manage Product Offering Exit</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Manage Product Offering Exit identifies an existing product offering which is unviable and manages the process to exit it from the market. It analyzes an existing product offering to identify if it is economically or strategically, identify customers impacted by any exit, develop customer specific or market segment exit or migration strategies, develop infrastructure transition and/or replacement strategies, and manage the operational aspects of the exit process. A business proposal identifying the competitive threats, risks and costs may be required as part of developing the exit strategy. It includes any interaction with cross-enterprise co-ordination and management functions to ensure that the needs of all stakeholders are identified and managed.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Identify Unviable Product Offering -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Identify Unviable Product Offering">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Identify Unviable Product Offering</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Not used for this process element</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Identify Product Offering Exit Impact -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Identify Product Offering Exit Impact">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Identify Product Offering Exit Impact</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Identify Product Offering Exit Impact identifies customers impacted by any exit, and develop customer specific or market segment exit or migration strategies.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Develop Product Offering Exit Strategies -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Develop Product Offering Exit Strategies">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Develop Product Offering Exit Strategies</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Develop Product Offering Exit Strategies develops infrastructure transition and/or replacement strategies, and manage the operational aspects of the exit process. A business proposal identifying the competitive threats, risks and costs may be required as part of developing the exit strategy. It includes any interaction with cross-enterprise co-ordination and management functions to ensure that the needs of all stakeholders are identified and managed.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Exit Product Offering from Market -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Exit Product Offering from Market">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Exit Product Offering from Market</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Exit Product Offering from Market removes a product specification, either by deleting it or indicating it is no longer valid. Notifications are sent to the Product Specification Development andamp; Retirement process so it can determine if the related specifications should also be removed. Additionally a notification may be sent to the Party Offering Development andamp; Retirement process so that it can determine if any on-boarded product offerings should also be removed.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Rollout/Launch Product Offering -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Rollout/Launch Product Offering">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Rollout/Launch Product Offering</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Rollout/Launch Product Offering supports the operational introduction of new processes and infrastructure to support a new or enhanced product offering and are responsible for conducting operations readiness testing and acceptance. It develops the procedures for the specific fulfillment, assurance and revenue generation processes and keeps them up to date. After successful testing, accept the new or enhanced process capabilities and manage a full-scale introduction for general availability.

Develop policy support and decision support knowledge for a product offering.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Develop Product Offering Procedures -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Develop Product Offering Procedures">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Develop Product Offering Procedures</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Develop Product Offering Procedures develops the procedures for the specific fulfillment, assurance and revenue generation processes for a new or enhanced product offering as well as keeping them up to date.

Develop policy support and decision support knowledge for these product offering processes and procedures.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Support Product Offering Operational Introduction -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Support Product Offering Operational Introduction">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Support Product Offering Operational Introduction</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Not used for this process element</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Conduct Operational Readiness Testing -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Conduct Operational Readiness Testing">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Conduct Operational Readiness Testing</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Not used for this process element</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Accept Product Offering Process Capabilities -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Accept Product Offering Process Capabilities">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Accept Product Offering Process Capabilities</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Not used for this process element</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Manage Product Offering Development -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Manage Product Offering Development">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Manage Product Offering Development</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Manage Product Offering Development ensures the co-coordinated delivery in line with the approved business case of all required product offering capabilities for that business case across the enterprise. These processes may use project management disciplines when a project is created to develop a new product offering to deliver the necessary capabilities, including process development, specific systems and network infrastructure developments, specific channel developments, specific operational procedures, and so forth. required to support the new product offering. 
Note that delivery of a product offering within the context of existing commercial agreements is managed through the Party Offering Development and Retirement process. If new partners are required, the Party Agreement Management process is used to deliver the necessary commercial agreements.
Note that the management of major new or enhanced infrastructure development to support Product and Offer Development is managed within the Product and Offer Capability Delivery process</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Product Offering Pricing -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Product Offering Pricing">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Product Offering Pricing</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Product Offering Pricing manages all aspects of pricing for product offerings. This includes standard pricing, policy-based pricing, algorithmic pricing, and feature/property-based pricing. Standard pricing processes set the price, develop pricing plans, update prices, obtain approval for pricing, provide notifications of price changes, and remove prices. 

The other types of prices define various forms of rules that determine what price should be used under certain conditions. For example, policy-based pricing may determine if a customer qualifies for a discount based on what product offerings are ordered, algorithmic pricing defines matrices of properties/features used to determine a price, feature/property-based pricing determines a price based on the selection of one or more properties or features by a customer.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Standard Product Offering Pricing -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Standard Product Offering Pricing">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Standard Product Offering Pricing</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Standard Product Offering Pricing sets the price, develops pricing plans, updates prices, obtains price approval, provides notifications of price changes, and removes prices. 

Prices are set for a variety of prices such as recurring, non-recurring, discounts, allowances. Pricing plans represent groupings of product offering prices, such as a plan composed of a recurring charge and a number of usage based charges. New, updated, and discontinued prices can go through an approval process if needed and notifications of them can be provided to internal and/or external parties such as customers and/or partners. Once a price lives its useful life it can be removed.

Note that the notification and approval processes can be reused by the other pricing related core processes for any additions, modifications, or removals associated with other types of prices whose lifecycles are managed by the other core processes into which the Product Offering Pricing process decomposes.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Set Product Offering Price -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Set Product Offering Price">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Set Product Offering Price</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Set Product Offering Price sets (creates) a variety of prices such as recurring, non-recurring, discounts, allowances. 

Price events that trigger a price are also defined by creating an event and associating it with a price. Additionally, the applicability of a price to one or more geographic areas are defined.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Create Product Offering Price -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Create Product Offering Price">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Create Product Offering Price</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Not used for this process element</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Define Product Offering Price Event -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Define Product Offering Price Event">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Define Product Offering Price Event</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Not used for this process element</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Associate Product Offering Price with Geographic Area -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Associate Product Offering Price with Geographic Area">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Associate Product Offering Price with Geographic Area</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Not used for this process element</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Develop Product Offering Pricing Plan -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Develop Product Offering Pricing Plan">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Develop Product Offering Pricing Plan</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Develop Product Offering Price Plan creates and modifies a grouping of product offering prices that represent a price plan for a product offering. For example a plan may consist of a recurring charge for a data plan and a charge for excess data usage.

Modification of the plan may include removing and adding product offering prices to the plan.

These processes interact with the Provide Product Offering Price Notification and Obtain Product Offering Price Approval processes to provide notifications of suggested new and changed price plans to parties who approve or are involved in some way, obtain approval to make them, then create or update the price. Once created or changed, notifications are sent to all involved parties, such as approvers, those consulted, and other involved parties.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Define Product Offering Price Plan -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Define Product Offering Price Plan">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Define Product Offering Price Plan</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Define Product Offering Price Plan creates a grouping of product offering prices that represent a price plan for a product offering. For example a plan may consist of a recurring charge for a data plan and a charge for excess data usage.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Modify Product Offering Price Plan -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Modify Product Offering Price Plan">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Modify Product Offering Price Plan</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Modify Product Offering Price Plan modifies a grouping of product offering prices that represent a price plan for a product offering. Included are the removal and addition of product offering prices to the plan.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Modify Product Offering Price -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Modify Product Offering Price">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Modify Product Offering Price</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Modify Product Offering Price suggests a change to a product offering price plan.

It interacts with the Provide Product Offering Price Notification and Obtain Product Offering Price Approval processes to provide notifications of suggested changes to parties who approve changes or have some other level of involvement, obtain approval to make the changes, and make the changes. Once changed, notifications are sent to all involved parties, such as approvers, those consulted about the changes, and other involved parties.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Suggest Product Offering Price Modification -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Suggest Product Offering Price Modification">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Suggest Product Offering Price Modification</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Not used for this process element</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Make Product Offering Price Modification -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Make Product Offering Price Modification">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Make Product Offering Price Modification</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Not used for this process element</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Obtain Product Offering Price Approval -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Obtain Product Offering Price Approval">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Obtain Product Offering Price Approval</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Obtain Product Offering Price Approval handles the approval of the creates, modifications, removals/discontinues to prices and price plans by those parties involved in the approval process. This includes any actions taken by any pricing related core processes.

Additionally enterprise cross-product pricing approval is also obtained.

Upon approval the Provide Product Offering Price Notification process provides notification of the approval to all involved parties.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Provide Product Offering Price Notification -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Provide Product Offering Price Notification">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Provide Product Offering Price Notification</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Provide Product Offering Price Notification issues notifications to involved parties of any new and change and discontinued product offering prices. Notifications are also made for any creates, changes, deletes made by other pricing related core processes.

It also identifies involved parties to whom notifications should be sent. These parties have been specified by the Manage Pricing Notification Involved Party process.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Manage Pricing Notification Involved Party -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Manage Pricing Notification Involved Party">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Manage Pricing Notification Involved Party</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Manage Pricing Notification Involved Party keeps track of individuals and organizations playing various roles who are involved in some way with product offering prices. Included is the type of involvement, such as those responsible for the approval process or those who should be informed about any pricing related activities.

This process communicates these, via a process flow, to the applicable Process Management andamp; Support process in the Enterprise domain which maintains the association between parties playing a variety of roles and the processes in which they are involved.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Issue Pricing Notification -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Issue Pricing Notification">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Issue Pricing Notification</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Not used for this process element</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Discontinue Product Offering Price -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Discontinue Product Offering Price">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Discontinue Product Offering Price</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Discontinue Product Offering Price discontinues a product offering price including a price plan. Discontinue may remove the price or plan or indicate that the price or plan is no longer valid.

It interacts with the Provide Product Offering Price Notification and Obtain Product Offering Price Approval processes to provide notifications of the discontinued price or plan to parties who are responsible for the approval of the discontinuance or have some other level of involvement, obtain approval to discontinue, and discontinue the price or plan. Once discontinued, notifications are sent to all involved parties, such as approvers, those consulted about the discontinuance, and other involved parties.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Policy-based Product Offering Pricing -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Policy-based Product Offering Pricing">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Policy-based Product Offering Pricing</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Policy-based Product Offering Pricing develops product offering pricing specific policy components used to determine the price of a product offering and to define cross-offering price policy rules. This process develops pricing specific product offering price policy conditions, actions, variables and values.

The price of a product is often dependent upon the procurement of another product for a particular price, another product offering, or another product offering of the same type. For example, if a premium software package is purchased then two from a choice of five other software packages are provided free.

As with other pricing processes this process interacts with the Provide Product Offering Price Notification and Obtain Product Offering Price Approval processes to provide notifications and gain approval of any actions taken by this process.

Note that this process is meant to use generic policy processes to define the base policy. These processes represent product offering pricing specific extensions to them. To date the generic processes have not yet been developed.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Develop Product Offering Price Condition -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Develop Product Offering Price Condition">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Develop Product Offering Price Condition</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Develop Product Offering Price Condition develops (creates, updates, and removes) a product offering price condition that represents a single constraint that defines how a policy rule is assessment.

A condition is part of a policy rule that is made up of a conditions and actions. Conditions and actions are defined by policy statements. For example a statement for a condition may be "If a premium software package is purchased".</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Develop Product Offering Price Action -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Develop Product Offering Price Action">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Develop Product Offering Price Action</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Develop Product Offering Price Action develops (creates, updates, and removes) a product offering price action that represents the outcome of the successful evaluation of one or more policy conditions. 

An action is part of a policy rule that is made up of a conditions and actions.  Conditions and actions are defined by policy statements.  For example a statement for an action may be "get two software packages from a choice of five for free".</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Develop Product Offering Price Variable -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Develop Product Offering Price Variable">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Develop Product Offering Price Variable</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Develop Product Offering Price Variable develops (creates, updates, and removes) a product offering price variable that represents a product offering, product offering price, or product specification type.

A variable is part of a policy that can be used to form a policy statement. The variable specifies an attribute or concept that should either be matched or in some way compared to a value when a condition is evaluated or set to some value when an action is taken. For example, "get two of five software packages".

If some cases the variables value is determined via the use of a derivation algorithm.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Develop Product Offering Price Value -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Develop Product Offering Price Value">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Develop Product Offering Price Value</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Develop Product Offering Price Value develops (creates, updates, and removes) a product offering price value that represents amount expressed in money or another medium of exchange for a product offering.

A value is part of a policy that can be used to form a policy statement. The value specifies an attribute that should either be set or cleared (if used in a policy action) or matched or compared in some way to a value of the policy variable in a policy condition. For example "get the two software packages for free (a zero price)".</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Manage Pricing Policy Association with Product Offering -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Manage Pricing Policy Association with Product Offering">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Manage Pricing Policy Association with Product Offering</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Not used for this process element</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Algorithmic Product Offering Pricing -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Algorithmic Product Offering Pricing">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Algorithmic Product Offering Pricing</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Algorithmic Product Offering Pricing develops (creates, modifies, deletes) a product offering pricing algorithmic matrix specification and the content of the matrix. The matrix is used to determine the price to charge/allow for a product that meet the criteria in the matrix, particularly for variable charges/allowances. For example, the amount to charge for data usage for some period.

Matrix specification development includes defining the matrix and its rows and columns. The rows and columns represent the criteria evaluated to determine the charge/allowance. They represent such things as types of product features/properties, types of product offering prices, algorithmic specific criteria such as type of customer, and so forth.

Matrix development defines a matrix based on a matrix specification, the content of matrix cells, as well as the product offering to which it applies. The cells represent the values for the product features/properties, such as excess data usage rates, product offering prices that will be charged/allowed, and values for algorithmic evaluation such as student, normal, or very important person (VIP) types of customers.

As with other pricing processes this process interacts with the Provide Product Offering Price Notification and Obtain Product Offering Price Approval processes to provide notifications and gain approval of any actions taken by this process.

Note that this process is meant to use/interact with generic property/feature processes to define them. To date the generic processes have not yet been developed.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Develop Algorithmic Product Offering Pricing Matrix Specification -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Develop Algorithmic Product Offering Pricing Matrix Specification">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Develop Algorithmic Product Offering Pricing Matrix Specification</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Develop Algorithmic Product Offering Pricing Matrix Specification defines (creates, modifies, and removes) the matrix and its rows and columns and other dimensions of a multi-dimensional matrix. The rows and columns represent the criteria evaluated to determine the charge/allowance. They represent such things as types of product features/properties, types of product offering prices, algorithmic specific criteria such as type of customer, and so forth.

Note that properties/features are also known as characteristic specifications.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Develop Algorithmic Product Offering Pricing Matrix Specification Definition -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Develop Algorithmic Product Offering Pricing Matrix Specification Definition">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Develop Algorithmic Product Offering Pricing Matrix Specification Definition</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Develop Algorithmic Product Offering Pricing Matrix Specification Definition develops (creates, modifies, and removes) the base product offering pricing matrix specification and associates it to the possible product offering(s) to which it applies.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Develop Algorithmic Product Offering Pricing Matrix Specification Structure -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Develop Algorithmic Product Offering Pricing Matrix Specification Structure">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Develop Algorithmic Product Offering Pricing Matrix Specification Structure</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Develop Algorithmic Product Offering Pricing Matrix Specification Structure defines  (creates, modifies, and removes) the structure of a product offering pricing matrix including its row(s)/columns and other dimensions of a multi-dimensional matrix as well as their sequence.

The rows and columns represent the criteria evaluated to determine the charge/allowance. They represent such things as types of product features/properties, types of product offering prices, algorithmic specific criteria such as type of customer, and so forth.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Develop Algorithmic Product Offering Pricing Matrix -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Develop Algorithmic Product Offering Pricing Matrix">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Develop Algorithmic Product Offering Pricing Matrix</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Develop  Algorithmic Product Offering Pricing Matrix defines (creates, modifies, and removes) a product offering pricing matrix based on a matrix specification, the content of matrix cells, as well as the specific product offering to which it applies. The cells represent the values for the product features/properties, such as excess data usage rates, product offering prices that will be charged/allowed, and values for algorithmic evaluation, such as student, normal, or very important person (VIP) types of customers.

Note that features/properties are also known as characteristic specification values.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Develop Algorithmic Product Offering Pricing Matrix Definition -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Develop Algorithmic Product Offering Pricing Matrix Definition">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Develop Algorithmic Product Offering Pricing Matrix Definition</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Develop Algorithmic Product Offering Pricing Matrix Definition defines the product offering pricing matrix based on a matrix specification and its association(s) to the specific product offering(s) to which it applies.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Develop Algorithmic Product Offering Pricing Matrix Cells -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Develop Algorithmic Product Offering Pricing Matrix Cells">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Develop Algorithmic Product Offering Pricing Matrix Cells</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Develop Algorithmic Product Offering Pricing Matrix Cells defines the content of the product offering pricing matrix cells. 

The cells represent the values for the product features/properties, such as excess data usage rates, product offering prices that will be charged/allowed, and values for algorithmic evaluation such as student, normal, or very important person (VIP) types of customers.

Note that features/properties are also known as characteristic specification values.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Feature/Property Product Offering Pricing -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Feature/Property Product Offering Pricing">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Feature/Property Product Offering Pricing</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Feature/Property Product Offering Pricing defines (creates, modifies, removes) simple to complex feature/property-based product offering pricing. Simple pricing is based on an association between one or more features/properties and a product offering price. For example, the price may vary based on the speed of internet connectivity. Complex pricing is defined by a group of features/properties upon which series of operations is performed to determine the price. For example, the price for a movie may be based on the title and format. A feature/property is also known as a characteristic.

As with other pricing processes this process interacts with the Provide Product Offering Price Notification and Obtain Product Offering Price Approval processes to provide notifications and gain approval of any actions taken by this process.

Note that this process is meant to use/interact with generic property/feature processes to define them. To date the generic processes have not yet been developed.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Develop Simple Feature/Property Product Offering Pricing -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Develop Simple Feature/Property Product Offering Pricing">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Develop Simple Feature/Property Product Offering Pricing</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Not used for this process element</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Develop Complex Feature/Property Product Offering Pricing -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Develop Complex Feature/Property Product Offering Pricing">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Develop Complex Feature/Property Product Offering Pricing</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Develop Complex Feature/Property Product Offering Pricing defines (creates, modifies, removes) a group of features/properties upon which series of operations is performed to determine the price. The series of operations defines an expression that when evaluated determines the price for the product offering. A feature/property is also known as a characteristic.

Single members of the group can be modified and/or removed as well as the entire group upon which the price is based.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Product Offering Cataloging -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Product Offering Cataloging">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Product Offering Cataloging</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Product Offering Cataloging develops a specification (definition) for a catalog containing product offerings, develops a product offering catalog, and exchanges a catalog among parties.

Product catalog specifications define reusable definitions for one or more catalogs. For example, a catalog specification that defines a catalog of smart home devices that is updated with new devices periodically and issued as a new catalog.

Product catalogs can be exchanged by sending a catalog to another party and receiving a catalog from another party. The receiving party could be a prospect, a customer, or another enterprise that may become a business partner that makes an enterprise's offerings available to the market. Similarly a catalog received from another party may be a prelude to the possible on-boarding of the parties offerings.

Note that this process reuses a set of generalized cataloging processes that can also be used to develop service catalogs and resource catalogs.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Develop Product Offering Catalog Specification -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Develop Product Offering Catalog Specification">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Develop Product Offering Catalog Specification</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Develop Product Offering Catalog Specification defines, updates, and removes the specification for a product catalog. It uses the generalized Develop Catalog Specification process to develop a specific type of catalog specification, in this case a product offering catalog specification.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Develop Product Offering Catalog -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Develop Product Offering Catalog">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Develop Product Offering Catalog</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Develop Product Offering Catalog defines, updates, and removes a product offering catalog. It associates a product offering and applicable product offering prices with a catalog. The product offering may have been developed by an enterprise or on-boarded from another party.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Define Product Offering Catalog -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Define Product Offering Catalog">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Define Product Offering Catalog</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Define Product Offering Catalog uses the generalized Develop Catalog process and its sub-processes to define, update, and remove a specific type of catalog, in this case a product offering catalog.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Associate Product Offering with Product Offering Catalog -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Associate Product Offering with Product Offering Catalog">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Associate Product Offering with Product Offering Catalog</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Associate Product Offering with Product Offering Catalog associates a product offering and applicable product offering prices with a catalog. The product offering may have been developed by an enterprise or on-boarded from another party.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Exchange Product Offering Catalog -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Exchange Product Offering Catalog">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Exchange Product Offering Catalog</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Exchange Product Offering Catalog exchanges a catalog with another party engaged in the value fabric. The exchange may be sending a product offering catalog to another party or receiving one from another party.

It uses the generalized Exchange Catalog process to exchange a catalog, in this case a product offering catalog.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Product Offering Agreement Management -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Product Offering Agreement Management">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Product Offering Agreement Management</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Product Offering Agreement Management develops a template agreement that defines the terms/conditions associated with a product offering. The terms/conditions are accepted by a party when the offering is acquired.

This process uses the general Party Agreement Management process to develop a template agreement. It's focus is on defining product offering terms/conditions, such as financial terms (which includes such things as acceptable methods of payment), shipment terms, and service term (which includes early termination fees). It also associates an offering and price(s) with the terms/conditions and with a template agreement.

Note that Party Agreement Management is also used to define template service level agreements and associate them to a product offering and/or a product specification.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Define Product Offering Agreement Terms/Conditions -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Define Product Offering Agreement Terms/Conditions">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Define Product Offering Agreement Terms/Conditions</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Define Product Offering Agreement Terms/Conditions defines product offering terms/conditions, such as financial terms (which includes such things as acceptable methods of payment), shipment terms, and service term (which includes early termination fees). 

The terms/conditions are accepted by a party when the offering is acquired.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Associate Product Offering and Price with Product Offering Agreement -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Associate Product Offering and Price with Product Offering Agreement">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Associate Product Offering and Price with Product Offering Agreement</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Not used for this process element</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Product Offering Prototyping -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Product Offering Prototyping">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Product Offering Prototyping</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Product Offering Prototyping iteratively develops a product offering. Product Offering Development andamp; Retirement processes develop each iteration of the offering to a state that enables it to be tested in some way by the Product Offering Development andamp; Retirements Conduct Product Offering Acceptance Testing process. Tests can be conducted internally, in the form of a pilot, or field trial. Tests are measured against defined acceptance criteria. Identified improvements/enhancements are made during the next iteration based on test results. Once the final iteration tests are accepted the offering is rolled out and launched to the market at large.

Note: This process is not further decomposed, because the process uses existing Product Offering Development andamp; Retirement processes.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Product Offering Promotion Development -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Product Offering Promotion Development">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Product Offering Promotion Development</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Product Offering Promotion Development develops a promotion for one or more product offerings delivered using different mediums (television, radio, print, online) that advertise the promotion to reach the market, customers and channels.

Product offering promotions can be designed with different ends in mind, including introducing a new product, retaining customers, bringing in new customers, and increasing sales of a product already on the market.

Product Offering Promotion Development works with other processes, such as Market Research, Marketing Campaign Management, Marketing Communications, and Advertising Management to design the promotion and advertising. One of the key roles of all these processes is to position the product in the market, especially versus competitive products.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Define Product Offering Promotion Scope -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Define Product Offering Promotion Scope">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Define Product Offering Promotion Scope</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Not used for this process element</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Ensure Product Offering Promotion Capability -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Ensure Product Offering Promotion Capability">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Ensure Product Offering Promotion Capability</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Ensure that there is capability (for example, information, materials, systems and resources) so that the product promotion can begin and managed. Monitor planned promotions and redistribute existing capability or enable new capability (people, facilities, infrastructure).</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Develop Product Offering Promotion -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Develop Product Offering Promotion">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Develop Product Offering Promotion</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Develop Product Offering Promotion manages all activities and stakeholder engagement to develop and agree on a product offering promotion and the selection of appropriate channel or channels to support delivery of the promotion. It also interacts with Marketing Communications to develop promotional messages and Marketing Campaign Management to associate promotions with a campaign.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Create Product Offering Promotion -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Create Product Offering Promotion">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Create Product Offering Promotion</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Not used for this process element</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Select Product Offering Promotion Delivery Channels -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Select Product Offering Promotion Delivery Channels">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Select Product Offering Promotion Delivery Channels</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Select Product Offering Promotion Delivery Channels selects the appropriate channel or channels to support delivery of a product offering promotion. A particular promotion may require selection of one or several delivery channels.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Obtain Product Offering Promotion Agreement -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Obtain Product Offering Promotion Agreement">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Obtain Product Offering Promotion Agreement</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Not used for this process element</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Start Product Offering Promotion -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Start Product Offering Promotion">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Start Product Offering Promotion</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Start Product Offering Promotion manages and co-ordinates the delivery of the product offering promotion to the selected channel(s). It ensures that the channel(s) (owned and/or contracted) are adequately trained and/or informed to manage the start of the promotion, and that sufficient resources are available in the selected channel(s) to support its start.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Manage Product Offering Promotion Channel Capability -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Manage Product Offering Promotion Channel Capability">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Manage Product Offering Promotion Channel Capability</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Not used for this process element</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Manage Product Offering Promotion Channel Resources -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Manage Product Offering Promotion Channel Resources">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Manage Product Offering Promotion Channel Resources</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Not used for this process element</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Wrap-up Start of Product Offering Promotion -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Wrap-up Start of Product Offering Promotion">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Wrap-up Start of Product Offering Promotion</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Wrap-up Start of Product Offering Promotion completes the start of the product offering promotion. It is coordinated with the delivery of the associated marketing campaigns and marketing communications.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Monitor Product Offering Promotion Effectiveness -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Monitor Product Offering Promotion Effectiveness">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Monitor Product Offering Promotion Effectiveness</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Monitor Marketing Campaign Effectiveness establishes metrics, monitors metrics, and analyzes metrics to gauge the effectiveness of a marketing campaign or campaigns. Based on analysis these processes feedback suggested changes to adapt the campaign or campaigns to become more effective now or in the future.

Note that this process' sub-processes reuse a generalized set of metric processes to develop, gather, and analyze (to some degree) marketing campaign metrics.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Develop Product Offering Promotion Metrics -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Develop Product Offering Promotion Metrics">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Develop Product Offering Promotion Metrics</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Not used for this process element</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Gather Product Offering Promotion Metrics -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Gather Product Offering Promotion Metrics">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Gather Product Offering Promotion Metrics</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Not used for this process element</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Analyze Product Offering Promotion Metrics -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Analyze Product Offering Promotion Metrics">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Analyze Product Offering Promotion Metrics</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Analyze Product Offering Promotion Metrics analyzes gathered product offering promotion(s) metrics to identify any issues with the promotion(s). The analysis includes identifying any established thresholds that have been crossed and the associated consequence (good or bad). A report is produced that reflects the effectiveness of the product offering promotion(s).</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Suggest Product Offering Promotion Change -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Suggest Product Offering Promotion Change">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Suggest Product Offering Promotion Change</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Suggest Product Offering Promotion Change feeds back suggested product offering promotion changes to adapt it to become more effective. This is based in part on the analysis of product offering promotion metrics.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Modify Product Offering Promotion -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Modify Product Offering Promotion">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Modify Product Offering Promotion</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Not used for this process element</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#End Product Offering Promotion -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#End Product Offering Promotion">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>End Product Offering Promotion</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Not used for this process element</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Undertake Product Offering Promotion Trend Analysis -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Undertake Product Offering Promotion Trend Analysis">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Undertake Product Offering Promotion Trend Analysis</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Not used for this process element</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Product Specification Test Development and Retirement -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Product Specification Test Development and Retirement">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Product Specification Test Development and Retirement</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Product Test Development andamp; Retirement is in charge of the Product Test catalog.
A type of Product Test aims at measuring proper functioning and capacities of a Product whatever the context is (Product Specification Development andamp; Retirement, Order Handling, Customer Order Orchestration, Product Performance Management, Customer Problem Handling, Product Test Management).
Product Test Development andamp; Retirement includes:
- Specifying in detail each Product Test according to the different context. It includes specifying:

	the roles authorized to use the Test and quotas for each type of role
	 the method to conduct the Test
	 the rules that define the strategies for conducting the test (including  the test plan)
	 the thresholds and related actions
	 the relationships with lower level tests (Service Test or Resource Test)
	the report of test results with rules for enrichment of Service andamp; Resource Tests results according to role asking for it

- Specifying test scenarios defining sequence of Tests with rules about context and planning to trigger it. It includes roles allowed for asking test scenario and corresponding quotas.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Product Capacity Management -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Product Capacity Management">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Product Capacity Management</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Product Capacity Management business process manages the activities required to ensure a business is able to plan, model, analyze, optimize, monitor and report product capacity, and related constraints according the commercial objectives in a timely and effective manner.
The underlying business activities supporting Product Capacity Management ensure that there is an effective understanding and management of Products Capacity in line with commercial demand and objectives, along with all the underlying production constraints.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Plan Product Capacity -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Plan Product Capacity">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Plan Product Capacity</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Plan Product Capacity business activity determine the design and organization of the production capacity management activities needed to meet changing demands for products over a period of time, as well as implement the plan for product capacity needs.
A Product's capacity plan ensures Product Management: 

	aligns capacity planning strategies with both commercial and operational goals,


	ensures that there are sufficient product capacity to support planned and forecasted commercial objectives,
	identifies gaps in capacity allocation early,
	determines product capacity needs according to demand,
	determines constraints and usage patterns over time,
	forecasts future capacity needs,
	and communicates products capacity requirements in time.

In the context of capacity planning, consideration is given to all input requirements, conversion processes and outputs when planning product capacity.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Align Product Capacity Planning Goals -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Align Product Capacity Planning Goals">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Align Product Capacity Planning Goals</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Align Product Capacity Planning Goals business activity is in charge of correlating the product capacity plans with business demand.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Establish Product Capacity GAP -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Establish Product Capacity GAP">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Establish Product Capacity GAP</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Establish Product Capacity GAP business activity identifies any disparity between product capacity goals and business objectives.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Forecast Product Capacity Need -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Forecast Product Capacity Need">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Forecast Product Capacity Need</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Forecast Product Capacity Need business activity develops projections that predict product capacity growth by understanding the impact on business.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Define Product Capacity Requirement -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Define Product Capacity Requirement">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Define Product Capacity Requirement</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Define Product Capacity Requirement business activity establishes, measures, and adjusts conditions that impact on planning product capacity for business expectations.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Establish Product Capacity Availability Timing Requirement -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Establish Product Capacity Availability Timing Requirement">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Establish Product Capacity Availability Timing Requirement</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Establish Product Capacity Availability Timing Requirement business activity identify scheduling needs for product capacity changes.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Implement Product Capacity Plan -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Implement Product Capacity Plan">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Implement Product Capacity Plan</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Implement Product Capacity Plan business activity is in charge of putting into effect the steps needed to achieve Product Capacity plans, with required product capacity, and product capacity management course of action.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Specify Required Product Capacity -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Specify Required Product Capacity">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Specify Required Product Capacity</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Specify Required Product Capacity business activity is in charge of implementing product capacity plans by identifying clearly and definitely product capacity expectations.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Specify Product Capacity Course of Action -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Specify Product Capacity Course of Action">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Specify Product Capacity Course of Action</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Specify Product Capacity Course of Action business activity identifies clearly and definitely sequence of activities that must be followed to meet 'product capacity plan' expectations.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Analyze Product Capacity -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Analyze Product Capacity">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Analyze Product Capacity</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Analyze Product Capacity business activity establishes and models insights, patterns and changes to product capacity, by assessing potential capacity and the actual capacity a product currently achieves.

This business activity covers collection of product-related data (usage data, performance data, operational data etc.) to support Product Managers to identify patterns and insights relating to a product.

Analyze Product Capacity support Product Capacity Management by providing relevant and timely insights, including available inventory holding capacity, products "time and material" capacity, etc. and how capacity utilization (allocated, in-use, unused) can be optimized to increase business value.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Identify Product Capacity Optimization Need -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Identify Product Capacity Optimization Need">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Identify Product Capacity Optimization Need</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Identify Product Capacity Optimization Need business activity establish the best, or most effective, use of product capacity.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Assess Available Product Capacity -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Assess Available Product Capacity">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Assess Available Product Capacity</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Assess Available Product Capacity business activity evaluates unused product capacity in relation to product capacity plans, and product utilization trends.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Model Product Capacity -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Model Product Capacity">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Model Product Capacity</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Model Product Capacity business activity establishes a representation of Product Capacity based on business defined properties.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Establish Product Capacity Utilization Behavior -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Establish Product Capacity Utilization Behavior">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Establish Product Capacity Utilization Behavior</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Establish Product Capacity Utilization Behavior business activity develops Product Capacity usage models.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Perform Product Capacity and Capacity Demand Trend Analysis -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Perform Product Capacity and Capacity Demand Trend Analysis">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Perform Product Capacity and Capacity Demand Trend Analysis</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Perform Product Capacity and Capacity Demand Trend Analysis business activity analysis trends between available product capacity and product capacity demand according to business and usage.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Optimize Product Capacity -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Optimize Product Capacity">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Optimize Product Capacity</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Optimize Product Capacity business activity enable improve Product use by managing underlying and related dependencies and constraints.
For Product Capacity Management, Optimize Product Capacity can enable reclaim unused Product capacity, allocate additional capacity just in time to meet demand, repurpose products based on capacity utilization patterns and support configuration management of constraints and dependencies.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Manage Product Capacity Utilization -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Manage Product Capacity Utilization">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Manage Product Capacity Utilization</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Manage Product Capacity Utilization business activity is in charge of fulfilling and assuring the effective use of product capacity.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Adjust Product Capacity -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Adjust Product Capacity">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Adjust Product Capacity</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Adjust Product Capacity business activity, fulfill changes to Product Capacity.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Allocate Product Capacity -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Allocate Product Capacity">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Allocate Product Capacity</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Allocate Product Capacity business activity assign the amount in capacity that a product can support.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Manage Product Capacity Thresholds -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Manage Product Capacity Thresholds">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Manage Product Capacity Thresholds</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Manage Product Capacity Thresholds business activity is in charge administering product capacity thresholds based on conditions that are bounded by operational concerns.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Monitor Product Capacity -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Monitor Product Capacity">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Monitor Product Capacity</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Monitor Product Capacity business activity identifies relevant Product Capacity attributes to track, and tracks all attributes, their use, and changes. 
Monitor Product Capacity supports all activities of Product Capacity Management by providing timely visibility for all concerns around Product Capacity.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Report Product Capacity -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Report Product Capacity">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Report Product Capacity</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Report Product Capacity business activity prepare and present detailed accounts on all relevant Product Capacity information, as deemed timely, relevant and reliable for use by business functions.
Different business functions with interest for Product Capacity may require specific reports with specific information. This business activity ensures Report Product Capacity business activity ensures information on Product Capacity is collated, organized and presented in forms useful and reliable to the needs of business functions in a timely manner.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Choose Product Offering to Purchase -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Choose Product Offering to Purchase">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Choose Product Offering to Purchase</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Choose Product Offering to Purchase chooses a product offering that is offered for purchase. One a choice is made the availability of the offering is provided.  The availability may be based on eligibility rules defined for the offering or its related product specification.  For example, if an offering is chosen, but is mutually exclusive with an offering already chosen then the chosen offering is not eligible for purchase.

Any terms/conditions associated with a product offering are also accepted, such as those for a contract or voucher.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Create Customized Product Offering to Purchase -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Create Customized Product Offering to Purchase">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Create Customized Product Offering to Purchase</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Create Customized Product Offering to Purchase develops a customized offering that may be a bundle. The content of the bundle may be based on rules defined for creating the customized offering. A price for the customized offering may also be determined (not chosen).</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Select Product Offering Purchase Quantity -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Select Product Offering Purchase Quantity">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Select Product Offering Purchase Quantity</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Not used for this process element.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Backorder Chosen Product Offering -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Backorder Chosen Product Offering">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Backorder Chosen Product Offering</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Backorder Chosen Product Offering provide the ability for a party making an inbound purchase to indicate that any quantity not available should be backordered. A notification is sent to the party when the offering is in stock.

Back ordering may involve splitting an item on the purchase into the quantity that is available and what is not available. Or the party making the purchase can change the quantity to what is available by using the Change Product Offering Purchase Selection process.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Product Inventory Management -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Product Inventory Management">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Product Inventory Management</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>The purpose of the Manage Product Inventory processes are twofold:

	Establish, manage and administer the enterprise's product inventory, monitor and report on the usage and access to the product inventory, and the quality of the data maintained in it. The product inventory maintains records of all products, their interactions with the enterprise, and any other product related
	Provide available Product Inventory related information required to support Fulfillment, Assurance and Billing andamp; Revenue processes.

The product inventory is also responsible for maintaining the association between customers and purchased product instances, created as a result of the Order Handling processes for a Product Specification in the context of a Product Offering.
Managing product inventory includes product creation, modification to the product inventory.
Responsibilities of these processes include, but are not limited to:

	Identifying the inventory-relevant information requirements to be captured for products;
	Identifying, establishing and maintaining product inventory repository facilities; 
	Establishing and managing the product inventory management and information capture processes;
	Managing the registration and access control processes that enable processes to create, modify and/or look up product information to and from the product inventory;
	Ensuring the product inventory repository accurately captures and records all identified product details, through use of automated or manual audits;
	Tracking and monitoring of the usage of, and access to, the product inventory repository and associated costs, and reporting on the findings;
	Identifying any technical driven shortcomings of the product inventory repository, and providing input to Resource Development andamp; Management processes to rectify these issues.
</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Identify Relevant Product Inventory Information -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Identify Relevant Product Inventory Information">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Identify Relevant Product Inventory Information</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Not used for this process element</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Maintain Product Inventory facilities -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Maintain Product Inventory facilities">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Maintain Product Inventory facilities</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Not used for this process element</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Control Product Inventory Access -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Control Product Inventory Access">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Control Product Inventory Access</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Not used for this process element</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Ensure Product Inventory Quality -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Ensure Product Inventory Quality">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Ensure Product Inventory Quality</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Ensuring the product inventory repository accurately captures and records all identified product details, through use of automated or manual audits. Monitoring and reporting on the quality of the information maintained in the inventory. The product inventory maintains records of all products, their interactions with the enterprise, and any other product related- information, required to support CRM and other processes. The product inventory is also responsible for maintaining the association between customers and purchased product instances, created as a result of the Order Handling processes.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Track Product Inventory Usage -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Track Product Inventory Usage">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Track Product Inventory Usage</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Not used for this process element</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Identify Product Inventory Shortcomings -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Identify Product Inventory Shortcomings">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Identify Product Inventory Shortcomings</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Not used for this process element</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Product Lifecycle Management Support -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Product Lifecycle Management Support">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Product Lifecycle Management Support</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Product Lifecycle Management Support supports the management of the lifecycle of a product and pricing associated with a product.
It can create a product, specify the involvement one or more parties have with it, updates information about the product including the status and relationships with Product Specification, Product Offering, Account and all related roles.

The lifecycle of a product also includes prices associated with it which are also managed by this process.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Product Lifecycle Administration Support -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Product Lifecycle Administration Support">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Product Lifecycle Administration Support</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Product Lifecycle Administration Support creates a product, specifies the involvement one or more parties have with it, updates information about the product including the status and relationships with Product Specification, Product Offering, Customer Account and all related roles at request from Operations processes.

Involvement may include the party account responsible for paying for the purchase and other charges, the party primarily responsible for the product, as well as users of the product. 

Updates may include adding new products to a bundle as well as the location of the product.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Create Product -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Create Product">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Create Product</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Create Product creates a product as a standalone product, a product bundle, or one that is part of a product bundle. The product is associated with either the product specification or product offering that describes it. If the product is one that is customized by a party and not offered by an enterprise the product is associated to the product specification that describes it.

Features/properties chosen during the Product Offering Purchasing process or chosen by this process if the product is created outside of the Product Offering Purchasing process may also be created for the product. This is done if the Product Configuration process is not used to create them.

A product is associated with its installation location if applicable and the associated product offering terms/conditions that were accepted, such as those for a contract or voucher. It may also be associated with one or more other products. For example, one product may replace another.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Specify Party Product Involvement -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Specify Party Product Involvement">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Specify Party Product Involvement</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Specify Party Product Involvement specifies the involvement one or more parties have with it and the party account that will pay for the product. If the product is paid for when it is purchased and there are no recurring or other types of charges due at some point in the future, then the party account may not be specified. Involved parties type of involvement is also specified, such as user, owner, payer. 

Additionally identity specific information, such as rights and restrictions, are specified for users (parties) of the product.

This process also updates and removes the involvement and identity specific information.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Modify Product -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Modify Product">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Modify Product</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Not used for this process element.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Product Pricing -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Product Pricing">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Product Pricing</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Product Pricing applies, updates a price associated with a product. A price may be applied when a party is browsing an enterprise's catalog (a form of window shopping that is supported by the Product Offering Purchase Lifecycle Management process), when configuring a product, or when purchasing a product offering.

The price may be what is paid when it is purchased or other types of charges due at some point in the future, such as recurring and usage based charges that are determined by a product's price.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Apply Product Price -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Apply Product Price">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Apply Product Price</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Apply Product Price applies a product price to a product. The price may be influenced directly or indirectly by a policy. A price may be a single price, a group of prices, or part of the group. For example, a group may consist of a recurring payment for base usage of the product, such as the number of times medical information can be sent to a doctor each month, and another price for any usage that exceeds the base.

The price may also be dependent on a policy or a policy may determine another price to apply to the product or some other product. For example, viewing more than a defined number of videos may result in a free view for a family member. Policies are defined when the product offering is developed and associated with an item on a product offering purchase.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Update Product Price -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Update Product Price">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Update Product Price</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Update Product Price makes changes to the price of a product. The update may include changes to associations with a policy that influences the price. This is typically triggered by changes to the price of a product offering in an enterprise's product catalog.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Product Usage Management -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Product Usage Management">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Product Usage Management</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>The Product Usage management processes encompass the functions required to guide, distribute, mediate, summarize, accumulate, and analyze Product Usage records. These processes may occur in real-time, near real-time (i.e. just at the end of the usage), or may be executed on a periodic basis.


Based on Service Usage, this process aims at identifying Product Usage. For example, for a Video on Demand where you can watch a video as many time as you want during 72 hours, several Service Usages might have been tracked (each time the user watches the video) and only one Product Usage will be identified for all Service Usages in the 72 hours after the first watch.

The guiding processes ensures that the Product Usage records used in the billing processes are appropriately related to the correct customer billing account and products. 

The Product Usage records are edited and if necessary reformatted (mediated) to meet the needs of subsequent processes. The billing event records may also be enriched with additional data during this process.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Product Usages -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Product Usages">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Product Usages</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>The Enrich Product Usages processes will augment the product usage records by adding data to the records from sources such as customer, product,  or other reference data.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Add Product Usage Data -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Add Product Usage Data">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Add Product Usage Data</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Not used for this process element.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Assign Product Usage Price -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Assign Product Usage Price">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Assign Product Usage Price</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Not used for this process element</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Guide and Assign Product Usages -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Guide and Assign Product Usages">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Guide and Assign Product Usages</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>The Guide Product Usages processes ensure that the event records used in the billing process relate to the correct customer billing account and products.  A specific product usage record may be related to multiple customer billing accounts and subscribed products. 
  
Distribution of product usage records to other processes may also occur.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Assign Product Usages -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Assign Product Usages">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Assign Product Usages</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Not used for this process element</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Distribute Product Usage -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Distribute Product Usage">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Distribute Product Usage</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Not used for this process element</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Guide Product Usages -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Guide Product Usages">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Guide Product Usages</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Guide Product Usages process is in charge of identifying Product Usages based on Service Usages.
For example, for a Video on Demand where you can watch a video as many time as you want during 72 hours, several Service Usages might have been tracked (each time the user watches the video) and only one Product Usage will be identified for all Service Usages in the 72 hours after the first watch.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Mediate Product Usages -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Mediate Product Usages">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Mediate Product Usages</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>The Mediate Product Usages process edits and reformats the data record to meet the needs of a recipient application.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Edit Product Usages -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Edit Product Usages">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Edit Product Usages</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Not used for this process element</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Reformat Product Usages -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Reformat Product Usages">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Reformat Product Usages</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Not used for this process element</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Report Product Usage Records -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Report Product Usage Records">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Report Product Usage Records</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>The purpose of the Report Product Usage Record processes is to generate reports on Product Usage records based on requests from other processes.
These processes produce reports that may identify abnormalities, which may be caused by fraudulent activity or related to customer complaints.
Investigation of problems related to these product usage records is also part of this process.

These processes also support other processes such as customer review of product usages (pre-billing and post-billing).</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Generate Product Usage Report -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Generate Product Usage Report">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Generate Product Usage Report</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Not used for this process element</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Investigate Product Usage Related Problem -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Investigate Product Usage Related Problem">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Investigate Product Usage Related Problem</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Not used for this process element</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Support Product Usage Related Process -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Support Product Usage Related Process">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Support Product Usage Related Process</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Not used for this process element</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Product Rating and Rate Assignment -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Product Rating and Rate Assignment">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Product Rating and Rate Assignment</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>The purpose of Product Rating and Assignment is to rate a value (monetary or other) to Product Usage or a set of Product Usages and assign the result to a Product and a Billing Account. The charge may be either a credit or a debit and can be handled either online or offline.

Online charging is performed in real-time, requiring an authorization component which may affect how the service is rendered and enables an operator to provide prepaid services to its customers. Whereas offline charging is performed after the service is rendered and is not required to be done in real-time and generally relates to subscription based products.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Perform Rating -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Perform Rating">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Perform Rating</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Process responsible for calculating the value of a product usage or a set of product usages, before, during or after the rendering of the service, based on parameters of the request (type, quantity, etc.), parameters of the customer/subscriber (tariffs, price plans, accumulated usage, contracts, etc.) and other parameters (time-of-day, taxes, etc.). The same request maybe rated differently for different subscribers based on their purchased offers or agreements.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Aggregate Items For Rate Assignment -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Aggregate Items For Rate Assignment">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Aggregate Items For Rate Assignment</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>This process is responsible for accumulating contributing items, which can be quantities, values (monetary or other) or both. Aggregation can occur over time or can be initiated to gather a snapshot of the items at a point in time.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Manage Customer Assignment Hierarchy -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Manage Customer Assignment Hierarchy">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Manage Customer Assignment Hierarchy</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Customer hierarchies are commonly used for corporate customers, family plans or other type of affinity groups. This process manages the assignment relationships among subscribers, e.g. sharing, inheriting or restricting balances, price plans and discounts. Thereby assuring that a charge is added to or subtracted from the correct account balance.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Provide Advice of Rate -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Provide Advice of Rate">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Provide Advice of Rate</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>The activity of Provide Advice of Rate (aka Advice of Charge) is responsible for providing advice on rates, in real-time or offline, an estimate or value of the rate for a specific usage request. The advice is usually based upon performing a full rating process for the request.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Apply Rate Level Discounts -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Apply Rate Level Discounts">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Apply Rate Level Discounts</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>This process applies discounts to product prices at an individual product level. A discount may be expressed as a monetary amount or percentage, and modifies a price for a product. When a discount is expressed as a percentage, the discounting process determines the discount calculated in relation to the price for the product.
  
The discount may be displayed as a separate entry on the bill or may be combined with the rate for the product to only show as one entry.
  
Discounts may be a one-time event or may have some duration (days, months, life of product, etc.). Discounts may apply to a specific customer or be generally available based on selection of products (for example - bundles). Discounting structures may involve tiers, tapers, or thresholds.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Product Balance Management -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Product Balance Management">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Product Balance Management</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>This process is responsible for holding, calculating, applying policies and managing functionality/interfaces for the Product balances 

Here the values resulting from rating and the application of discounts are applied to a Product balance. The balance affected by the value may be monetary or other balances such as minutes, points, or tokens. Authorizing service requests based on available balance is optional.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Manage Product Balance Containers -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Manage Product Balance Containers">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Manage Product Balance Containers</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>This process manages the balance containers assigned to a Product and is used to keep track of usage events, providing input for decision making processes (such as product usage authorization) by means of the balance policies. 

The containers include monetary and non-monetary balances (or shared) and are used as prepaid balances (enabling real-time product usage authorization), postpaid balances (in conjunction with an Account-Receivables [AR] application). Examples of non-monetary balances and allowances are: free minutes, WAP-only quota, etc.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Manage Product Balance Policies -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Manage Product Balance Policies">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Manage Product Balance Policies</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Product Balance policies are rules that describe how balance affecting usages are to be handled.  This is done  by comparing the value of each usage against criteria such as the following:
- a minimum allowable balance limit (e.g. balance must remain above zero), 
- balance expiration dates, 
- balance thresholds actions and notifications and
- roll-over and cyclic policies.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Product Balance Operations Management -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Product Balance Operations Management">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Product Balance Operations Management</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Product Balance operations processes the charged events, using balance policies and then guides the results towards the relevant balance containers. Operations include :
- Reserving amounts from any balance for any session, and crediting unused reservations back into the balance, when a session is released. 
- Updating balances by applying charges to the balance and credit/debit adjustments.
- Balance queries.
- Transferring amounts from one balance to another.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Authorize Transaction Based on Product Balance -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Authorize Transaction Based on Product Balance">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Authorize Transaction Based on Product Balance</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>This process may include Product balance reservation and must be performed online. 
Subsequent balance updates are not required to be done in real-time. In this context a usage is provided by the network, e.g. voice call. Product might be a digital content delivered via the network, e.g. content such as music, games, etc.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Product Catalog Planning Management -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Product Catalog Planning Management">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Product Catalog Planning Management</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Product Catalog Planning Management business process covers a set of business activities that understand and enable establish the plan to define, design and operationalize a catalog in order to meet the needs and objectives of Product cataloging.
The Product Catalog Planning Management business process ensure that the organization is able to identify the most appropriate scheme and goal for it catalog. It includes designing the Catalog plan and developing the specification according to Product management requirement.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Design Product Catalog Plan -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Design Product Catalog Plan">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Design Product Catalog Plan</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Product Design Catalog Plan business activity understands requirements and capabilities demanded from the business to establish the Catalog plan based on the Product strategy for Product Catalog Planning Management.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Define Product Catalog Specification -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Define Product Catalog Specification">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Define Product Catalog Specification</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Define Catalog Specification business activity establishes the Catalog specifications based on the product/service/resource strategy to support Catalog Planning Management.
Define Catalog Specification leverages Specification Management business activities to establish the mandatory and optional design requirements, as well as catalog entry fields according to product/service/resource management needs. This process will be governed by the Enterprise Business Process for Catalog Management.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Product Catalog Lifecycle Management -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Product Catalog Lifecycle Management">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Product Catalog Lifecycle Management</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Catalog Lifecycle Management business process covers a set of business activities that enable manage the lifecycle of an organizations catalog from design to build according to defined requirements.
Catalog Lifecycle Management proves the overarching governance to manage all the stages in the realization and operationalization of the Product/Service/Resource Catalog in support of the organizations business goals.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Manage Product Catalog Design -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Manage Product Catalog Design">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Manage Product Catalog Design</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Manage Catalog Design business activity cover the design of the Catalog in accordance to the Catalog Management Lifecycle.
Manage Catalog Design business activity will leverage Catalog Specification requirement for all information (features, attributes etc.) to be managed by the catalog in order to enable support the Catalog Lifecycle Management.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Manage Product Catalog Build -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Manage Product Catalog Build">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Manage Product Catalog Build</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Manage Catalog Design business activity covers the design of the Catalog in accordance to the Catalog Management Lifecycle.
This business activity leverages input from the Catalog Design to construct the product/service/resource Catalog in order to meet the business operations goals.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Manage Product Catalog Policy -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Manage Product Catalog Policy">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Manage Product Catalog Policy</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Manage Catalog Build business activity establishes, manages and administers the governing of the catalog for operations readiness and operations.
This business activity leverages support of the Enterprise governance processes for product/service/resource catalog lifecycle management.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Product Catalog Operational Readiness Management -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Product Catalog Operational Readiness Management">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Product Catalog Operational Readiness Management</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Product Catalog Operational Readiness Management business process establishes and administers the support needed to operationalize Product catalogs for ongoing day-to-day business needs.
These business activities implement the Product Catalog through Release and Deploy business activities.
Release Product Catalog business activity ensure all cross-functional activities needed to support catalog maintenance and operations, such as training and updating the support of the catalog are in place.
Release Product Catalog business activity includes identifying stakeholders, catalog integration, catalog federation etc. for any scenario in support of the organizations business goals, including Release conditions that support users, customers and business partners.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Release Product Catalog -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Release Product Catalog">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Release Product Catalog</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Release Product Catalog business activity ensure all cross-functional activities needed to support catalog maintenance and operations, such as training and updating the support of the catalog are in place.
Release Product Catalog business activity includes identifying stakeholders, catalog integration, catalog federation etc. for any scenario in support of the organizations business goals, including Release conditions that support users, customers and business partners.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Plan and Schedule Product Catalog Release -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Plan and Schedule Product Catalog Release">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Plan and Schedule Product Catalog Release</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Plan and Schedule Product Catalog Release business activity is used to handle the release plan for the Product Catalog.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Control Product Catalog Release -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Control Product Catalog Release">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Control Product Catalog Release</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Control Product Catalog Release business activity is used to support the various catalog release tasks.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Test Product Catalog -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Test Product Catalog">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Test Product Catalog</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Test Product Catalog business activity is used to establish the quality, reliability and performance requirement of the catalog according to the Product management needs.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Deploy Product Catalog -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Deploy Product Catalog">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Deploy Product Catalog</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Deploy Product Catalog business activity manage the availability and use of the Product catalog in operations.
Deploy Product Catalog business activity includes identifying stakeholders, creating catalog category hierarchies, catalog integration, and catalog federation for any scenario, such as with business partners and between business functions.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Product Catalog Content Management -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Product Catalog Content Management">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Product Catalog Content Management</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Product Catalog Content Management business process define and provide the business activities that support the day-to-day operations of Product Catalogs in order to realize the business operations goals.
Product Catalog Content Management business processes include administering the Product Catalog instance in production, maintaining catalog entries, assuring catalogs, managing catalog access, managing entry lifecycle through versioning, handling catalog entity entry and changes, supporting distribution of catalogs as needed, and supporting user-facing activities.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Maintain Product Catalog Content -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Maintain Product Catalog Content">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Maintain Product Catalog Content</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Maintain Product Catalog Content business activity handles catalog content entry through adding or updating the Catalog by following the established Catalog Content Management standards and policies.
Manage Catalog Entry support the following activities and sub-activities:
Maintaining Catalog Content Versions
Maintain Catalog Content Relationship
Maintain Catalog Content taxonomy 
Organize Catalog Entry
Classify Catalog Entry</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Maintain Product Catalog Content Version -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Maintain Product Catalog Content Version">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Maintain Product Catalog Content Version</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Maintain Product Catalog Content Version business activity handles tracking and controlling changes for Product catalog entries.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Maintain Product Catalog Content Relationship -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Maintain Product Catalog Content Relationship">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Maintain Product Catalog Content Relationship</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Maintain Product Catalog Content Relationship business activity handles associating Product catalog entries.
Catalog Content Relationship for Product catalog entries can be internal and external to the Product, Service or Resource domains.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Maintain Product Catalog Content Entry -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Maintain Product Catalog Content Entry">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Maintain Product Catalog Content Entry</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Maintain Product Catalog Content Entry business activity handles content entry, content organization, content classification in the Product Catalog according to the Product Catalog model.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Organize Product Catalog Content Entry -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Organize Product Catalog Content Entry">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Organize Product Catalog Content Entry</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Organize Product Catalog Content Entry business activity handles Catalog Content organization according to the Product Catalog model.
Organize Catalog Content Entry business activities can include ordering, arranging, sorting, assembling, and grouping.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Classify Product Catalog Content Entry -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Classify Product Catalog Content Entry">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Classify Product Catalog Content Entry</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Classify Product Catalog Content Entry business activity specifically handles Catalog Content organization according to business classification characteristics for the Product Catalog.
Classify Product Catalog Content Entry is specific to shared qualities or characteristics defined by the organization.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Manage Product Catalog Access -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Manage Product Catalog Access">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Manage Product Catalog Access</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Manage Product Catalog Access business activity handles access to the catalog according to the Catalog Content Management standards and policies.
Manage Product Catalog Access will handle assigning catalog managers and granting privileges.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Manage Product Catalog Content Lifecycle -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Manage Product Catalog Content Lifecycle">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Manage Product Catalog Content Lifecycle</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Manage Product Catalog Content Lifecycle business activity handles changes to catalog content according to the Catalog Content Management standards and policies.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Distribute Product Catalog -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Distribute Product Catalog">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Distribute Product Catalog</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Distribute Product Catalog business activity handles exchange and distribution of catalogs according to the Catalog Content Management standards and policies.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Product Specification Management -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Product Specification Management">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Product Specification Management</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Product Specification Management business process leverages captured product requirements to develop, master, analyze, and update documented standard and personalized conditions that must be satisfied by product design and/or delivery.
Product Specifications Management can result in establishing, in a centralized way, technical (know-how) standards for products. Such standards provide the organization with a means to control and approve the values and inputs of product specification through structure, review, approval and distribution processes to users (including customers and business partners).</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Describe Product Specifications -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Describe Product Specifications">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Describe Product Specifications</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Describe Product Specifications business activity identify and elaborate on the conditions for meeting product requirement in order to support assuring consistency, quality, functionality and fit for purpose products.
Describing Product Specification can leverage captured product requirements and product preferences to build in tolerances for changes according to users of the products.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Describe Product Specifications Property -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Describe Product Specifications Property">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Describe Product Specifications Property</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Product Specification Property enumerate all the product specification attributes and their units, and documents requirements that provides product teams the information they need to build out or enhance features or functionality of products.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Align Product Specifications -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Align Product Specifications">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Align Product Specifications</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Align Product Specifications business activity handle the alignment, relationships and linkages of product specification to functional and non-functional requirement.
The alignment of product specifications can be to other products as well as realization of the specific services and resource according to business objectives (e.g. cost, other accounting and non-accounting requirements etc.).</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Model Product Specifications -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Model Product Specifications">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Model Product Specifications</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Model Product Specification business activity is in charge of determining independent product specifications variables to include and exclude from asserting the product's specification relationships and connections.

The need for modelling product specifications often begins when a product manager seeks to define the relationship between independent product variables and the dependent product variable.
This business activity is used by organizations to establish and manage the collection of standardized, pre-documented product specifications and their dependencies to guide Lifecycle Management and Operations.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Analyze Product Specifications -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Analyze Product Specifications">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Analyze Product Specifications</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Analyze Product Specifications business activity research, assess and evaluate performance criteria and factors to develop, master, control and update in products specifications, according to ongoing requirements.
This business activity can include multiple analyzes of product specifications, including standard analysis (based on empirical research) or custom analysis (based on other standards). Analysis of Service Specification include testing product specifications, and the ability to meet business requirements, as well as conformance to operational mandates.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Update and Version Product Specifications -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Update and Version Product Specifications">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Update and Version Product Specifications</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Update Product Specification business activity updates, tracks and versions changes to existing product specifications according to versioning policies to support product requirement management and product's operational activities.
This business activity manages all changes to product specifications over their lifecycle. As part of this business activity, Product Specification versioning is a sub-activity which ensures communicating changes to product specifications, so that product planners and consumers know what to expect. It includes communicating when changes are made to product specification properties.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Product Anomaly Lifecycle Management -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Product Anomaly Lifecycle Management">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Product Anomaly Lifecycle Management</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Product Anomaly Lifecycle Management business process establishes and controls all activities that are involved in overseeing, directing, administering, controlling and organizing the definition, detection/prediction, mitigation and learnings related to Product Anomaly Management.
Product Anomaly Lifecycle Management cover the lifecycle activities, including:
Establishing what is normal for a active product (buy, sell, care) in order to inform deviations or aberrations.
Orchestrating Product Anomaly Management activities to meet customer and business partner needs.
Managing the ability to acquire and apply knowledge and skills from past and present product anomalies.
Managing actions that make the best or effective use of Product Management Closed Loops.
Monitoring feedback to and from Product Management to support Product Anomaly Management activities.
Reporting on Product Anomaly Management Closed Loops.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Manage Product Anomaly Definition -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Manage Product Anomaly Definition">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Manage Product Anomaly Definition</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Manage Product Anomaly Definition business activity is in charge of defining and describing the information about data which is used in Product Anomaly Management. 
Product Manage Anomaly Definition business activity covers activities that describe the criteria, characteristics, and expectations of information required for Product Anomaly Detection. Any descriptions and definitions of the information about data use in Product Anomaly Management business activities may include, but not be limited to "normal pattern data", "constraints data", "goals data" etc.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Define Product Anomaly Closed Loop -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Define Product Anomaly Closed Loop">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Define Product Anomaly Closed Loop</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Define Product Anomaly Closed Loop business activity state and describe the Product Anomaly Closed Loops along with associated information that lead to identifying, detecting or predicting a Product Anomaly.
This business activity supports Anomaly definition process and the Closed Loops associated, including all associated inputs that reasonably affect the management of an Anomaly Lifecycle. This activity also ensures that the organization understands, and has well-defined operational workflows underpinning Anomaly Management.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Establish Product Anomaly Closed Loop Information Sources -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Establish Product Anomaly Closed Loop Information Sources">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Establish Product Anomaly Closed Loop Information Sources</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Establish Product Anomaly Closed Loop Information Sources business activity identifies all information sources and the requisite data that must be managed to support Product Anomaly Management Closed Loops.
Establish Product Anomaly Closed Loop Information Sources help to identify the information (not limited to business and operations rules), business logic, levels of classification (by importance, by period etc.), impact and urgency etc. that can help detect Product Anomaly. This process supports Product Anomaly Management during day-to-day operations.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Orchestrate Product Anomaly Management Closed Loop -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Orchestrate Product Anomaly Management Closed Loop">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Orchestrate Product Anomaly Management Closed Loop</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Orchestrate Product Anomaly Management Closed Loop business activity is in charge of organizing, arranging and coordinating changes that control Product Anomaly Closed Loops.
This business activity will cover:
Managing Product Anomaly Detection activities - initiating, suspending, maintaining, and terminating.
Organizing Product Anomaly Detection activities - including arranging the sequence for Closed Loop activities.
Coordinating changes to a Product Anomaly Management Closed Loop.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Manage Product Anomaly Profile -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Manage Product Anomaly Profile">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Manage Product Anomaly Profile</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Manage Product Anomaly Profile business activity is in charge of recording and analyzing Product Anomaly Management frameworks in order to enable assess and predict Anomaly Management capabilities according to well-specified models.
Manage Product Anomaly Profile supports Product Anomaly Management operations, as well as capturing the business intents that need to be associated with Product Anomaly Closed Loops and Product Anomaly Management Lifecycle.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Monitor Product Anomaly Management Closed Loop -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Monitor Product Anomaly Management Closed Loop">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Monitor Product Anomaly Management Closed Loop</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Monitor Product Anomaly Management Closed Loop business activity provides the capability to observe Product Anomaly Management Closed Loops.
This business activity helps to scan; watch; monitor; gain awareness of Product Anomaly Management activities that close the loop in an Product Anomaly Management Lifecycle(s).</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Report Product Anomaly Management Closed Loop -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Report Product Anomaly Management Closed Loop">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Report Product Anomaly Management Closed Loop</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Report Product Anomaly Management Closed Loop business activity documents information organized to deliver an account of any, and all Product Anomaly Closed Loops.
Anomaly Closed Loops may fall into either or across any of the four stages in any of the overarching Closed Loop pattern - Observe, Orient, Decide and Act - or other variations.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Manage Product Anomaly Intelligence -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Manage Product Anomaly Intelligence">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Manage Product Anomaly Intelligence</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Manage Product Anomaly Intelligence business activity is in charge of acquiring and applying new learning, knowledge and skills to Product Anomaly Management.
This business activity supports improving, optimizing, or evolving Product Anomaly Management activities. Manage Product Anomaly Intelligence helps to incorporate new knowledge and skills into Product Anomaly Management processes. This is as well to enable improvement and optimization of Anomaly Management in a continuum.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Manage Product Anomaly Optimization -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Manage Product Anomaly Optimization">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Manage Product Anomaly Optimization</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Manage Product Anomaly Optimization business activity is in charge of actions that make the best and most effective use of Product Anomaly Management activities to improve Product Anomaly Management.
Manage Product Anomaly Optimization business activity can manage the business logic and business rules associated with Product Anomaly Detection, Product Anomaly Assessment, Product Anomaly Forecasting and Prediction, Product Anomaly Mitigation, as well as underlying Product Knowledge Management.
This business activity also includes fine-tuning of business logic, operations logic, business and operations rules that improve efficiency of Anomaly Management as a whole.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Product Anomaly Management -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Product Anomaly Management">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Product Anomaly Management</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Product Anomaly Management business processes establish actions that predict and detect aberrations or outlier events/activities, assess them for their impact, mitigate them, and record them before they ever become product problem management concerns. 
By establishing that an action or event is abnormal (based on known patterns), Product Anomaly Management helps to assess them through a set of activities that may triage, plan detailed assessment, classify them and provide  mitigatory actions for them. Through Product Anomaly Management, assurance of Products, based on abnormal events or activities can be well categorized, prioritized and actioned on. Product Anomaly Management is different from Product Problem Management as the later addresses known issues, faults or problems.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Predict Product Anomaly -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Predict Product Anomaly">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Predict Product Anomaly</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Predict Product Anomaly business activity is in charge of declaring or indicating in advance (or foretells on the basis of product buy-use-sell observation, product use experience or reason) upcoming exceptions, as well as trends that can lead to outlier activities / events or problems.
Product Anomaly Prediction business activity can help to detect and interpret early activities or events with their impending exceptions while suggesting causes.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Forecast Product Anomaly -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Forecast Product Anomaly">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Forecast Product Anomaly</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Forecast Product Anomaly business activity predicts future Product anomaly along with implications using historical, and /or ongoing patterns observed through exceptions.
Forecast Product Anomaly business activity may include what-if analysis, or impact analysis of the anomalous exceptions. Forecast Product Anomaly business activity supports the identification of potential risks of an exception, and the course of action needed to avoid potential risks.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Detect Product Anomaly -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Detect Product Anomaly">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Detect Product Anomaly</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Detect Product Anomaly business activity identify Product (buy/use/care) activities that are a deviation (aberrations or abnormal actions/events) from well-define norms or expectations.
Product Anomaly Detection finds patterns in Product Management activities, as well as with engaged parties given a deviation from planned, or expected business objectives or goals.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Identify Product Exception -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Identify Product Exception">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Identify Product Exception</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Identify Product Exception business activity supports the detection of Product Anomaly by investigating (recognizing and establishing) particular activity or event as an exception.
Identify Product Exception business activity will support all Product Anomaly Management business activities - Assess Product Anomaly, Predict Product Anomaly, Mitigate Product Anomaly and Learn Product Anomaly.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Treat Product Exception -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Treat Product Exception">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Treat Product Exception</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Treat Product Exception business activity provides the set of actions that support managing a products anomalous exception.
This covers actions that may be:
Proactive: Where the treatment of the conditions leading from the exception are controlled;
Reactive: Where the treatment is directly in response to the exception.
Treat Product Exceptions business activity helps to outline a series of actions that can expedite decisions for mitigation.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Escalate Product Exceptions -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Escalate Product Exceptions">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Escalate Product Exceptions</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Escalate Product Exception business activity is in charge of increasing the attention given to handling of a Product Exception.
Escalating a Products exception may be based on several factors, including defined business rules of escalation, or the lack thereof for handling a products exception.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Assess Product Anomaly -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Assess Product Anomaly">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Assess Product Anomaly</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Assess Product Anomaly business activity check, estimate, appraise and evaluate Product anomaly observations to determine implications and follow-on treatment.
Assess Product Anomaly ensures that the business can ascertain understanding of a products anomalous activity, its extent/scale, cause and effect, and provide evidence-based information to develop courses of action.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Triage Product Exception -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Triage Product Exception">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Triage Product Exception</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Triage Product Exception business activity is in charge of identifying and assigning the degrees of urgency, and the order of treatment of products anomalous exceptions.
Triage Product Exceptions sub activities may include prioritizing exceptions and underlying product anomaly events while examining causes that enable apply an initial set of mediatory actions.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Plan and Select Product Anomaly Assessment Criteria -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Plan and Select Product Anomaly Assessment Criteria">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Plan and Select Product Anomaly Assessment Criteria</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Plan and Select Product Anomaly Assessment Criteria business activity define the course of action to assess a product anomaly, along with organizing the products anomaly assessment criteria in order to best facilitate detection and mitigation of anomalies.
The 'Plan and Select Assessment Criteria' process helps the organization to optimize the approaches to assess product anomaly criteria in order to continually avoid impact of false positives and false negatives in the detection of product anomalies.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Analyze Product Anomalies to Learning -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Analyze Product Anomalies to Learning">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Analyze Product Anomalies to Learning</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Analyze Product Anomalies to Learning business activity establish actions to discover and correlate anomalous behavior to 'learned normal' or 'expected behavior'.
Analyze Product Anomalies to Learning sub activities help to enrich the organization's Anomaly Detection activities altogether, which can result in a reduction in the time to detect, triage and treat product anomalies.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Classify Product Anomaly -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Classify Product Anomaly">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Classify Product Anomaly</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Classify Product Anomaly business activity establish ways to organize product anomalies into established categories according to business priorities and product management objectives.
Classify Product Anomaly includes establishing robust classification models that help to triage anomalies, determine communication needs, determine and measure impact, and report on product anomalies.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Manage Product Anomaly Assessment Feedback Reporting -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Manage Product Anomaly Assessment Feedback Reporting">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Manage Product Anomaly Assessment Feedback Reporting</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Manage Product Anomaly Assessment Feedback Reporting business activity is in charge of establishing and handling the activities that prepare and report the feedback based of Product Anomaly Assessment activity.
Manage Product Anomaly Assessment Feedback business activity covers tasks that prepare and report feedback of an Anomaly Assessment activity. This business activity is also helpful in supporting the optimization of the Anomaly Detection business activity, such as fine-tuning know-how for product anomaly detection.
Reports generated from this business activity can be utilized for Product Anomaly Mitigation and can help to select the consequent actions required to mitigate a product anomaly.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Mitigate Product Anomaly -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Mitigate Product Anomaly">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Mitigate Product Anomaly</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Mitigate Product Anomaly business activity is in charge of allaying or alleviate the impact of a products anomalous exception.
Mitigate Product Anomaly identify and coordinate mitigatory actions required for products anomalous exceptions, including the initiation of remedial actions, and providing support to monitor and report on the mitigatory action.
Mitigate Product Anomaly can ensure the effect of a detected anomalous exception is minimized or resolved through appropriate actions. The aim of this business activity is to reduce Product Problem Management occurrence.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Identify Product Exception Mitigation -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Identify Product Exception Mitigation">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Identify Product Exception Mitigation</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Identify Product Exception Mitigation business activity helps to map products anomalous exceptions with actions that will reduce impact to business.
Identifying product exception and their mitigatory action involves tasks that may leverage established business policies and constraints, and/or be based on knowledge and skills related to context.
This business activity helps to incorporate the right treatment based on the importance, impact or risk factors involved in a products operation. Any treatment of this nature can be static, based on pre-defined business rules, or dynamic based on skills and knowledge derived from context.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Coordinate Product Exception Mitigation -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Coordinate Product Exception Mitigation">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Coordinate Product Exception Mitigation</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Coordinate Product Exception Mitigation business activity is in charge of managing the different activities of an exception mitigation plan all together to successfully realize a mitigation plan.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Initiate Product Exception Mitigation -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Initiate Product Exception Mitigation">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Initiate Product Exception Mitigation</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Initiate Product Exception Mitigation business activity is in charge of starting the correct activities that mitigate product anomaly exceptions, cognizant of business requirement and goals.
Initiate Product Exception Mitigation actions include recommendations for course of actions, fostering dynamic execution of actions, and/or scheduling actions based on predetermined business conditions and policies.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Monitor Product Exception Mitigation -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Monitor Product Exception Mitigation">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Monitor Product Exception Mitigation</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Monitor Product Exception Mitigation business activity is in charge of  observing, checking and keeping a continuous records of mitigatory actions that support Product Anomaly Management.
Monitor Product Exception Mitigation covers the action and data that are involved (including collection and analysis on predefined set of information e.g. KPIs etc.) in Product Anomaly Management business activities, tasks and workflows.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Report Product Exception Mitigation -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Report Product Exception Mitigation">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Report Product Exception Mitigation</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Report Product Exception Mitigation business activity is in charge of providing an account (documented or otherwise) of mitigatory actions taken to lessen or reduce the impact of a product anomaly.
Reporting on Product Exception Mitigation may follow well-defined business and operations criteria, or predefined set of metrics (KPIs etc.) that are underlying to mitigate anomaly business activity.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Manage Product Anomaly Learning -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Manage Product Anomaly Learning">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Manage Product Anomaly Learning</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Manage Product Anomaly Learning business activity is in charge of capturing, or acquiring knowledge and skill related to handled anomalous exceptions (from detection, through assessment to mitigation).
Manage Anomaly Learning business activity ensure that knowledge and skills gained from product anomalies can aide future Product Anomaly Management activities.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Manage Product Anomaly Case History -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Manage Product Anomaly Case History">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Manage Product Anomaly Case History</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Manage Product Anomaly Case History business activity records all past information on Product Anomaly events, Product Anomaly Management activities and data underlying, and representing Product Anomaly cases.
Manage Product Anomaly Case History includes the maintenance of past and present records, all artifacts, knowledge-base (e.g. the specifications, profiles, exception patterns, action patterns etc.) and versioned information.
This business activity supports the organization to maintain skills and learning repository to identify and predict Anomalous Exception patterns and mitigatory actions.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Product Problem Management -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Product Problem Management">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Product Problem Management</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Product Problem Management process is in charge of directing and controlling activities that identify, triage, discover causes, report and close product problems (cases, issues, challenges and faults etc.). 

Product Problem Management ensures that products that are commercially offered by the organization can be assured to meet the goals and objectives of their design. The objective of this processes is to respond to product challenges/concerns/issues/cases and offer answers/resolution to them. 

The goal of this process is mediate the impact, or resolve the concerns that impact Marketing and Sales objectives.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Identify Product Problem -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Identify Product Problem">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Identify Product Problem</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Identify Product Problem business activity is in charge of establishing a product case/concern/issues or challenge. 

Identify Product Problem includes activities that clearly define product problem and collect information that relevantly described the existence of the problem. 
This business activity may include tasks that measure or assess problem to determine whether a problem (i.e., discrepancy) exists.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Define Product Problem -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Define Product Problem">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Define Product Problem</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Define Product Problem business activity is in charge of describing a product problem.

This business activity supports identifying product problem by leveraging collected product  information to clearly describe the product problem for subsequent resolution.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Collect Product Problem Information -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Collect Product Problem Information">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Collect Product Problem Information</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Collect Product Problem Information business activity is in charge of gathering all data/information that enable establish a product problem.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Triage Product Problem -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Triage Product Problem">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Triage Product Problem</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Triage Product Problem business activity is in charge of organizing product problems based on business defined conditions to support analyzing and managing problem closure. 

Triage Product Problem includes tasks that categorize product problems in order to effectively prioritize handling according to their impact on business.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Categorize Product Problem -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Categorize Product Problem">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Categorize Product Problem</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Categorize Product Problem business activity is in charge of organizing and classifying product problems based on business conditions. 

Categorize Product Problem helps to cluster and correlate product problems in order to support triaging product problems with product problem solutions (if they exist solutions in the knowledge base.)</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Prioritize Product Problem Management -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Prioritize Product Problem Management">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Prioritize Product Problem Management</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Prioritize Product Problem business activity is in charge of ordering product problems by level of urgency and impact based to the business. 

Prioritize Product Problem business activity supports Categorize Product Problem in order to effectively Triage Product Problem.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Analyze Product Problem -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Analyze Product Problem">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Analyze Product Problem</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Analyze Product Problem business activity is in charge of investigating product problems, discovering product problem cause and providing relevant reports to outline problem product cause.

This business activity is key to identify appropriate solutions to product problems, and inform the right plan of action to resolve product problems.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Investigate Product Problem -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Investigate Product Problem">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Investigate Product Problem</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Investigate Product Problem business activity is in charge of observing and identifying the cause of a product problem. 

Investigate Product Problem includes tasks that study and examine product problems and associated information in order to discover product problem cause.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Report Product Problem Cause -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Report Product Problem Cause">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Report Product Problem Cause</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Report Product Problem Cause business activity in charge of providing documented (written or verbal) evidence of the cause of a product problem.

This business activity supports Investigate Product Problem to present the analysis of a product problem.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Discover Product Problem Cause -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Discover Product Problem Cause">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Discover Product Problem Cause</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Discover Product Problem business activity is in charge of obtaining evidence of the investigation of the product problem.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Manage Product Problem Solution -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Manage Product Problem Solution">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Manage Product Problem Solution</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Manage Product Problem Solution business activity is in charge of directing and controlling activities that establish solutions to resolve product problems.

Manage Product Problem Solution includes activities that identify and define all product problem solutions, establish course of action for resolving product problems according to solutions, reviewing product problem solutions to be effective, implement established plans for resolving or correcting product problems and reporting on implementation of product problem solutions.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Define Product Problem Solution -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Define Product Problem Solution">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Define Product Problem Solution</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Define Product Problem Solution business activity is in charge of finding and describing solutions and solution goals to the product problem.

This business activity acts to identify a set of solutions to a product problem each with well-described goals. Goals may be strategic or tactical.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Plan Product Problem Solution -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Plan Product Problem Solution">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Plan Product Problem Solution</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Plan Product Problem Solution business activity is in charge of identifying tasks and actions that enable implement answers or correction to a product problem.

This business activity ensures that the set of actions and tasks to resolve or solve a product problem solution meet the solution goals. 
a set of solutions to a product problem. evidence of the investigation of the product problem.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Implement Product Problem Solution -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Implement Product Problem Solution">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Implement Product Problem Solution</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Implement Product Problem Solution business activity is in charge of executing the set of tasks identified to address or correct product problem.

Implement Product Problem Solution ensures that plans and their goals match business expectations.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Review Product Problem Solution -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Review Product Problem Solution">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Review Product Problem Solution</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Review Product Problem Solution business activity is in charge of inspecting and authorizing a product problem solution. 

This business activity ensures that from the set of problem solutions defined, the most appropriate that fits the goals of the business are implemented.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Validate Product Problem Solution -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Validate Product Problem Solution">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Validate Product Problem Solution</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Validate Product Problem Solution business activity is in charge of assuring the answer or corrective measures applied to resolve or mediate a product problem are accepted.

This business activity includes tasks that test the product problem solution, communicate with parties impacted by a product problem and liaising with activities that implement and report product problem solution.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Report Product Problem Solution -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Report Product Problem Solution">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Report Product Problem Solution</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Report Product Problem Solution business activity is in charge of documenting (written or verbal) the answer or corrective actions applied to resolve or mediate a product problem.

This business activity includes tasks that design product problem handling status reports, collecting information relevant to report product problem solutions,  development of the product problem solution report, review of the product problem reports fit-for-purpose, and distributing product problem reports.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Close Product Problem -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Close Product Problem">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Close Product Problem</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Close Product Problem business activity is in charge of finalizing all activities that resolve or correct a product problem and updating product problem knowledge base to formally end a product problems lifecycle.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Update Product Problem Knowledge Management -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Update Product Problem Knowledge Management">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Update Product Problem Knowledge Management</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Update Product Problem Knowledge Management business activity is in charge of adding or enhancing the product problem knowledge-based with all new activities and related information about the instance of product problem management. 

This business activity includes tasks the collect information related to the identification of the product problem, outcome of analyses of the product problem, and providing answers or corrective actions to resolve the product problem.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Collect Market Problem Information -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Collect Market Problem Information">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Collect Market Problem Information</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Collect Market Problem Information business activity is in charge of gathering relevant and related data and information that are directly or correlateable to a defined market problem.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Define Market Problem -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Define Market Problem">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Define Market Problem</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Define Market Problem business activity is in charge of establishing a clear case for a market issue, challenge or concern.  

Define Market Problem includes tasks that establish the market issue/challenge or concern and the impact it has on the business.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Customer Order Processing Management -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Customer Order Processing Management">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Customer Order Processing Management</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Product Order Management business direct and control processes that capture, track, fulfil, deliver and close product order requests. 

Product Order Management begins with the capture of a product order request based on a party (Customer, Business Partner, Employee etc.), and processes, tracks and reports the products from order capture to  fulfilment, shipping the order, and manaing cancellation and returns.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Manage Product Order Capture -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Manage Product Order Capture">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Manage Product Order Capture</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Manage Product Order Capture business activity direct and control the creation of product orders, validate product orders against feasibility and/or availability checks, and ensure product orders are complete for onward business processing.

Manage Product Order Capture assures for completeness, the Product Order requirements needed for succssfuly processing, delivering and managing returns of orders.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Manage Product Order Selection -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Manage Product Order Selection">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Manage Product Order Selection</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Manage Product Order Selection business activity directs and controls the addition and change to product orders. 
Manage Product Order selection ensures product order requirement details and applied information is complete.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Add Product Order Requirement -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Add Product Order Requirement">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Add Product Order Requirement</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Add Product Order Requirement business activity captures and includes new product related items into a product order request. 

Add Product Order Requrement includes activities to add product items with their associated details (such as variants etc.) to the product order, which includes assigning product item quantities, and providieng information to characterize the need for customization of the product ("Make-to-Order"; "Configure-to-Order").</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Add Product Item -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Add Product Item">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Add Product Item</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Add Product Item business activity adds new product related items (product lines, version etc.) to the product order.

Add Product Item enables product orders of varieites of product based on business defined unit of acquisition. This business activity helps the business offer and support product variations.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Assign Product Item Quantity -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Assign Product Item Quantity">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Assign Product Item Quantity</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Assign Product Item Quantity business activity defines the units of quantity for every product item. 

Assign Product Item Quanity ensures minimum and maxium quantities that may apply to a product item within a given product order.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Customize Product Order -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Customize Product Order">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Customize Product Order</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Customize Product Order business activity supports product ordering for products that can be customized or personalized. 

Customize Product Order enables the business to offer products that are unique and built-to-order. This includes making products have different variants, with different settings and configurations.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Change Product Order Requirement -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Change Product Order Requirement">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Change Product Order Requirement</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Change Product Order Requirement business activity is responsible for enabling and applying changes to the requirement of a product order. 

Change Product Order Requirement ensures changes to product items, modification of product order item quantities and removal of products order requirements.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Change Product Item -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Change Product Item">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Change Product Item</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Change Product Item business activity is responsible for adjusting product order items in a product order requirement. 

Change Product Item supports 'Change Product Order Requirement' by enabling product items to be modified according to business rules and policies supporting the product ordering lifecycle.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Modify Product Order Item Quantity -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Modify Product Order Item Quantity">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Modify Product Order Item Quantity</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Modify Product Order Item Quantity business activity is responsible for adjusting quantities of product order items in a product order requirement. 

Modify Product Order Item Quantity supports 'Change Product Order Requirement' by enabling product item quantities are modified according to business rules and policies supporting the product ordering lifecycle.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Remove Product Order Requirement -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Remove Product Order Requirement">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Remove Product Order Requirement</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Remove Product Order Requirement business activity is responsible for taking out or deleting product order requirement.  

Remove Product Order Requirement supports 'Change Product Order Requirement' by enabling product orders can be effectively moved from the valid or active or available product order schedule or queue.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Approve Product Order -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Approve Product Order">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Approve Product Order</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Approve Product Order business activity is responsible for certifying that a product order, based on defined product order management business rules and policies, can be endorsed for further processing. 

Approve Product Order business activity supports 'Manage Product Order Capture' to accept the product order according to business rules and policies. This business activity also supports the de-risk of product order placements or reduce impact on the integrity of the product ordering process.

This business activity includes actoins that determine pre-purchase feasibility for the delivery of the products.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Validate Product Order Requirement Availability -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Validate Product Order Requirement Availability">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Validate Product Order Requirement Availability</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Validate Product Order Requirement Availability business activity is responsible for checking and proving the validty of new product order requirements. 

Validate Product Order Requirement Availability ensure the business accepts product order that meet defined product order management requirements, business rules and policies, and can that can be honored.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Approve Product Order Processing -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Approve Product Order Processing">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Approve Product Order Processing</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Approve Product Order Processing business activity is responsible for officially accepting the product orders for processing. 

Approve Product Order Processing supports 'Approve Product Order' business activity to make the business initiate processing of the ordr. This business activity ensures the business is able to, and accountabe to actions to honor the order.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Manage Product Order Fulfillment -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Manage Product Order Fulfillment">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Manage Product Order Fulfillment</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Manage Product Order Fulfillment business activity is responsible of directing and controlling for product orders, the configuration of product order fulfilment steps, managing the product order fulfilment profile, managing the product order picking and packing, managing product order shipment, managing product order returns, tracking product order fulfilment, and closing fulfilment of product orders.

Manage Product Order Fulfillmenti support "Product Order Management" by ensuring all assocated products, and/or services and/or resources are organized to meet the required promise of the product order.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Manage Product Order Fulfillment -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Manage Product Order Fulfillment">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Manage Product Order Fulfillment</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Manage Product Order Fulfillment business activity is responsible of directing and controlling for product orders, the configuration of product order fulfilment steps, managing the product order fulfilment profile, managing the product order picking and packing, managing product order shipment, managing product order returns, tracking product order fulfilment, and closing fulfilment of product orders.

Manage Product Order Fulfillmenti support "Product Order Management" by ensuring all assocated products, and/or services and/or resources are organized to meet the required promise of the product order.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Configure Product Order fulfilment -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Configure Product Order fulfilment">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Configure Product Order fulfilment</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Configure Product Order fulfilment business activity is responsible for processing the activities to receive products for a product order , processing product orders, and arranging all supporting requirements of a product order to meet the expectations of the product order.

Configure Product Order Fulfilment supports "Manage Product Order Fulfilment" activity to facilitate processing of product order placements, and managing the arrangements to support the returns of products for product orders.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Make to Product Order -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Make to Product Order">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Make to Product Order</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Make to Product Order business activity is responsible for all arrangement to make products based on product order.

Make to Product Order business activity supports the business to offer customized products. This business activity supports 'manage product order fulfillment' by ensuring there is a fulfillment plan in place to faciliate custmized products in a product order.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Assemble to Product Order -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Assemble to Product Order">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Assemble to Product Order</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Assemble to Product Order business activity is responsible for all arrangement to put together  products based on product order.

Make to Product Order business activity supports the business to build or construct products in a product order. This business activity supports 'manage product order fulfillment' by ensuring there is a fulfillment plan in place to faciliate putting together requirements in a product order.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Schedule Product Order Fulfilment -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Schedule Product Order Fulfilment">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Schedule Product Order Fulfilment</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Schedule Product Order Fulfilment business activity is responsible for  making a plan for fulfilling a product order according to the product order. 

Schedule Product Order Fulfilment supports 'manage product order fulfilment' by ensuring appropriate prioritization and "resources" available to faciliate processing the delivery of a product order.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Manage Product Order Fulfilment Profile -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Manage Product Order Fulfilment Profile">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Manage Product Order Fulfilment Profile</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Manage Product Order Fulfilment Profile business activity direct and control product order fulfilment actions that take a product from order to delivery. 

Manage Product Order Fulfilment Profile supports 'manage order fulfilment' with planning, design, analyzing and checking that product order fulfiment contain requirements (related product order type, product order payment related-information etc. ) that control where, how and what information is needed for fulfiling product order. The requirement  manage product pre-orders and product backorders.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Manage Product Preorder -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Manage Product Preorder">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Manage Product Preorder</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Manage Product Preorder business activity direct and control Product Pre-orders which are product orders that are taken for products that are not yet available. 

Manage Product Preorder supports 'Manage Product Order Fulfilment Profile' by providing businesses with input to plan production effectively.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Manage Product Backorder -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Manage Product Backorder">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Manage Product Backorder</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Manage Product Backorder business activity directs and controls placement of product orders where the business has insufficient product capacity or product-related supplies. 

Manage Product Backorder enables 'manage product order fulfilment profiles' that effectively estimate demand, manage capacity and supplies in a proactive way to support sudden increases in product orders.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Manage Product Order Picking/Packing -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Manage Product Order Picking/Packing">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Manage Product Order Picking/Packing</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Manage Product Order Picking/Packing directs and controls all activities that enable product order picking and product order packing. 

Manage Product Order Picking/Packing creates product order picking and packing requirements for a product order to support the product order delivery process.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Manage Product Order Picking/Packing Rule -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Manage Product Order Picking/Packing Rule">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Manage Product Order Picking/Packing Rule</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Manage Product Order Picking/Packing Rule business activity directs and controls the regulations that define or restrict actions that guide packing and picking activities. 

Manage Product Order Picking/Packing Rule ensures that the right picking and packing procedures are in place to support all product orders accepted for product order delivery. Picking/packing rules may be defined for single product orders, batch product orders, zone-based product orders etc.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Pick Product Order Item -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Pick Product Order Item">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Pick Product Order Item</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Pick Product Order Item business activity identifies and collects product items according to a product order from where they are stored in readiness to satisfy the product order fulfilment process.

Pick Product Order Item includes activities like sorting (sort while pcking, or sort after pick) and ensures that all the types of picking for all types of products can be completed according to the product order management requirements. Pick Product Order Item can apply to piece picking, case picking, single order picking, batch picking, wave picking, pallet picking etc.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Package Product Order Item -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Package Product Order Item">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Package Product Order Item</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Pack Product Order Item business activity is responsible for packaging all the product order items into the business approved shpping standard. 

Pack Product Order Item ensures all the items in a product order can be appropriately organized for product order delivery process, along with all information needed to assure successfull delivery.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Manage Product Order Shipment -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Manage Product Order Shipment">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Manage Product Order Shipment</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Manage Product Order Shipment business activity directs and controls the activities to prepare the product order for shipment using the packing information, generating product order manifest and managing the shipping activities of the products in the product order. 

Manage Product Order Shipment includes activities that create the shipment, update shipment, select the sales orders for shipment, verify sales orders for product items in the product order, confirm the shipment details, hold shipment, generate manifests, delete shipments, cancel shipments as well as providing all information that are required for the shipment.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Manage Product Order Shipping Profile -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Manage Product Order Shipping Profile">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Manage Product Order Shipping Profile</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Manage Product Order Shipping Profile business activity directs and controls the activities to set shipping procedures and rules, as well as business rates for shipping products orders.

Manage Product Order Shipping Profile ensures that product orders for shipping can be managed  systematically, as well as accounted for by the business throgh related product-based shipping rules and rates.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Manage Product Order Shipping Rule -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Manage Product Order Shipping Rule">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Manage Product Order Shipping Rule</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Manage Product Order Shipping Rule business activity directs and controls the definition and management activities for Product Order Shipping procedures and rules.

Manage Product Order Shipping Rule include rules that may be specific for, say, products and locations or both.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Manage Product Order Shipping Rate -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Manage Product Order Shipping Rate">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Manage Product Order Shipping Rate</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Manage Product Order Shipping Rate business activity directs and controls the definition and management Product Order Shipping rates. 

Manage Product Order Shipping Rate address custom and pre-defined shipping rate for product order shipping profiles.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Manage Product Order Returns -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Manage Product Order Returns">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Manage Product Order Returns</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Manage Product Order Returns business acitivity directs and controls activities that process or reject a return of a product order.

Manage Product Order Returns includes activities to reverse product orders, authorize product order returns, receive returned product order items, close prodict order returns according to the business rules established for product management.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Create Reverse Product Order Return -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Create Reverse Product Order Return">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Create Reverse Product Order Return</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Create Reverse Product Order Return business activity is responsible for generating reverse orders for previously delivered product orders. 

Create Reverse Product Order ensures there is a correlation between product orders delivered and product order returns in accordance to the business rules and policies for product management.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Manage Product Order Shipping -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Manage Product Order Shipping">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Manage Product Order Shipping</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Manage Product Order Shipping business activity directs and controls the activities to alert product order consignee before arrival of goods at destination containing the details of product order shipment. 

Manage Product Order Shipping includes Receiving the processed product order, processing the shipping order, and fulfilling the shipping order.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Create Product Order Shipment Advice -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Create Product Order Shipment Advice">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Create Product Order Shipment Advice</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Create Product Order Shipment Advice business activity is responsible for creating the alert given by the prodict ordr shipper to the product order consignee before arrival of theproduct order.

Create Product Order Shipment Advice helps consignees to track product orders.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Schedule Product Order Shipment -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Schedule Product Order Shipment">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Schedule Product Order Shipment</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Schedule Product Order Shipment business activity is responsible for supporting the product order delivery by providing schedule 

Schedile Product Order Shipment helps to plan out shipments and deliveries in advance based on the organizations supply chain and customer demand.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Authorize Product Order Return -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Authorize Product Order Return">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Authorize Product Order Return</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Authorize Product Order Return business activity is responsible for permitting a product order reverse order to be processed.  

Authorize Product Order Return ensures that product order returns are acceptable and valid according to product ordering rules.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Receive Returned Product Order -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Receive Returned Product Order">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Receive Returned Product Order</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Receive Returned Product Order business activity is responsible for accepting and processing the product order return.   

Receive Returned Product Order ensures that product order returns are compliant with product order return policies.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Close Product Order Return -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Close Product Order Return">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Close Product Order Return</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Close Product Order Return business activity is responsible for ensuring communication and confirmation of product order returns with conginees. 

Close Product Order Return ensures that all activities to ensure the closure of product order return are completed successfully.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Track Product Order Fulfilment -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Track Product Order Fulfilment">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Track Product Order Fulfilment</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Track Product Order Fulfilment business activity records all the product order fulfilment processing status.

Track Product Order Fulfilment supports detecting early evidence of "something going wrong" or not according to business rules and polcies for a product order accepted for fulfilment. It supports escalation of product order fulfilment challenges and remediation.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Close Product Order Fulfilment -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Close Product Order Fulfilment">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Close Product Order Fulfilment</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Close Product Order Fulfilment business activity finalizes a product order fulfillment to be complete. 

Close Product Order Fulfilment supports successful product order delivery can take place to essure the business can meet the obligations for product order management.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Manage Product Order Delivery -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Manage Product Order Delivery">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Manage Product Order Delivery</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Manage Product Order Delivery business activity directs and controls the activities to validate products in the product order. 

Manage Product Order Delivery business activity ensures product can be successfuly be supplied to consignee of the product order to enable complete the product order process.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Validate Product Order Delivery Requirement -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Validate Product Order Delivery Requirement">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Validate Product Order Delivery Requirement</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Validate Product Order Delivery Requirement business activity proves validity of the delivery requirements in the product order. 

Validate Product Order Delivery Requirement checks to ensure that a given product order has delivery requirement that conform to consignee expectations in the product order.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Deliver Product Order -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Deliver Product Order">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Deliver Product Order</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Deliver Product Order business activity is responsible for the actual delivery activity of the product order fulfilled by the business to the consignee. It includes ensuring the product order can be activated/is actiated, tracking the product order delivery and notifying product order delivery. 

Deliver Product Order ensures that the chosen channel and delivery plan based on business rules and/or requirement of the consignee are followed in the actual delivery to the consignee.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Activate Product Order Items -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Activate Product Order Items">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Activate Product Order Items</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Activate Product Order Item business activity is responsible for making a product order item active. 

Activate Product Order is available when an order is either ready to be shipped or provisioned. This business activity may require the consignee to initiate the request for activation through a request/response interaction, or by getting the product provisiion at the time of shipping.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Track Product Order Delivery -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Track Product Order Delivery">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Track Product Order Delivery</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Track Product Order Delivery business activity is responsible for tracing or following up with the status and stages in the a product order delivery acivity.

Track Product Order enables the organization and product order consignees to effectively know the status of product order in a the product order delivery stage.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Notify Product Order Delivery -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Notify Product Order Delivery">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Notify Product Order Delivery</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Notify Product Order Delivery business activity is responsible for sending information or alerts/advice on product product order delivery stages or to advice the product order delivery completion. 

Notify Product Order Delivery ensures there is communication at all times during the product order delivery stage.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Close Product Order Delivery -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Close Product Order Delivery">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Close Product Order Delivery</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Close Product Order Delivery business activity is responsible for ensuring communication and confirmation of product order delivery with conginees. 

Close Product Order Delivery ensures that all activities to ensure the closure of product order delivery are completed successfully.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Manage Product Order Cancellation -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Manage Product Order Cancellation">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Manage Product Order Cancellation</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Manage Product Order Cancellation business activity directs and controls the product order cancellation requests. 

Manage Product Order Cancellation ensures that product order requests are processed in accordance to the organizations business rules and policies. It includes managing request of product order cancellation, processing product order cancellation, and tracking product order cancellation.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Request Product Order Cancellation -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Request Product Order Cancellation">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Request Product Order Cancellation</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Request Product Order Cancellation business activity enables product orders to be dropped or removed from product order processing. 

Request Product Order Cancellation ensures that there is a process in place within the organization product order process to address requests that are legitimate or acceptable by the organizations business rules and policies.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Manage Product Order Cancellation -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Manage Product Order Cancellation">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Manage Product Order Cancellation</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Manage Product Order Cancellation business activity is responsible for directing and controlling the product order cancellation approval, rejection or completion of the cancellation. 

Manage Product Order Cancellation ensures that product order cancellation requests can be reviewed before acceptance based on the organizations business rules and policies, and for such cancellation requests to be processed according to product order cancellation policies.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Review Product Order Cancellation -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Review Product Order Cancellation">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Review Product Order Cancellation</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Review Product Order Cancellation business activity is responsible for assessing a product order cancellation request can be honored by the business. 

Review Product Order Cancellation ensures that canellation requests meet the product order cancellation policies established for product order management.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Reject Product Order Cancellation -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Reject Product Order Cancellation">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Reject Product Order Cancellation</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Reject Product Order Cancellation business activity is responsible for disqualifying or dismissing a product order cancellation request. 

Reject Product Order Cancellation ensures that requestors are adequately adviced and understand product order cancellation terms and conditoins. The process ensures the business rules and policies for product order management are used in support of product order cancellation rejection.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Complete Product Order Cancellation -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Complete Product Order Cancellation">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Complete Product Order Cancellation</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Complete Product Order Cancellation business activity is responsible for concluding the processing of product order cancellation requests.

Complete Product Order Cancellation ensures that information and actions necessary to finalize the product order cancellation are complete.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Track Product Order Cancellation -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Track Product Order Cancellation">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Track Product Order Cancellation</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Track Product Order Cancellation business activity is responsible for following up product order cancellation stages and states within the stages. 

Track Product Order Cancellation ensures that product order cancellations are followed and their states at all stages can be traced and accounted for.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Close Product Order Cancellation -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Close Product Order Cancellation">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Close Product Order Cancellation</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Close Product Order Cancellation business activity is responsible for ensuring communication and confirmation of product order cancellation conginees. 

Close Product Order Cancellation ensures that all activities to ensure the closure of product order cancellation are completed and acknowledged by the consignee.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Manage Product Order Management Reports -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Manage Product Order Management Reports">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Manage Product Order Management Reports</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Manage Product Order Management Reports business activity directs and controlls monitoring of product order management activities, notify product order management status and reporting product order management activities. 

Manage Product Order Management Reports ensures that there is visibility of product order management altogether in order to ensure product order management meet the organization's business requirements.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Monitor Product Order Management Activity -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Monitor Product Order Management Activity">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Monitor Product Order Management Activity</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Monitor Product Order Management Activity is responsible for observing and recording every activity in the product order management process.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Notify Product Order Management Status -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Notify Product Order Management Status">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Notify Product Order Management Status</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Notify Product Order Management Status business activity is responsible for sending information about product order management activities.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Report Product Order Management Activity -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Report Product Order Management Activity">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Report Product Order Management Activity</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Report Product Order Management business activity is responsible for formally accounting for product order management.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Manage Product Order Search -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Manage Product Order Search">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Manage Product Order Search</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Manage Product Order Search business activity directs and controls product order browsing and discovery.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Browse Product Orders -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Browse Product Orders">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Browse Product Orders</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Browse Product Orders business activity is resposible for making product order available based on general or multiple information.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Find Product Orders -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Find Product Orders">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Find Product Orders</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Find Product Orders business activity is responsible for specifically locating and accessing product orders based on specific information.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Customer Readiness and Support -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Customer Readiness and Support">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Customer Readiness and Support</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Customer Readiness andamp; Support processes ensure the support capability is in place to allow the Customer Fulfillment, Assurance and Billing processes to operate effectively.  
The responsibilities of these processes include, but are not limited to:
- Provision of sales customer process infrastructure 
- Policy support and decision support knowledge for customers and customer interactions (including billing activities)
-Maintaining inventories to support the customer data required by the FAB and CRM OSandamp;R processes 
- Monitoring and reporting on the capabilities and costs of the individual Customer FAB processes
- Longer-term trend analysis on customer FAB processes in order to establish the extent to which enterprise targets for these processes are being achieved and/or the need for the processes to be modified.
These processes support the operational introduction of new processes and infrastructure to support new and/or enhanced customer management capabilities and are responsible for conducting operations readiness testing and acceptance. They develop the procedures for the specific Fulfillment, Assurance and Billing processes and keep them up to date. After successful testing, these processes accept the new or enhanced process capabilities and manage a full-scale introduction for general availability.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Support Customer Interface Management -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Support Customer Interface Management">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Support Customer Interface Management</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>The purpose of the Support Customer Interface Management processes is to ensure that there is capability (for example, information, materials, systems and resource) so that the Customer Interface Management processes can operate effectively when a contact with a customer occurs. Examples are information on how to handle unusual requests based on temporary situations, systems needed to accept and track customer contacts, requests for the provisioning of additional resources where it has been identified that current levels will impact on timely contact handling.
These processes are responsible for implementing generic and specific changes to customer interfaces. This support could be in updating agent scripts, IVR announcements, Web pages, etc. Customer Interface Support processes keep up to date all information concerning customers.
These processes undertake trend analysis on customer contacts, e.g. type, frequency, duration, outcome.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Ensure Customer Interface Capability -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Ensure Customer Interface Capability">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Ensure Customer Interface Capability</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>element Ensure that there is capability (for example, information, materials, systems and resource) so that the Customer Interface Management processes can operate effectively when a contact with a customer occurs. Examples are information on how to handle unusual requests based on temporary situations, systems needed to accept and track customer contacts, requests for the provisioning of additional resources where it has been identified that current levels will impact on timely contact handling. These processes are responsible for implementing generic and specific changes to customer interfaces. This support includes localization support and personalization support, and it could be in updating agent scripts, IVR announcements, Web pages, etc. Customer Interface Support processes keep up to date all information concerning customers.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Undertake Customer Contacts Trend Analysis -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Undertake Customer Contacts Trend Analysis">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Undertake Customer Contacts Trend Analysis</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Not used for this process element</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Support Customer Order Management -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Support Customer Order Management">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Support Customer Order Management</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>The purpose of the Support Order Management processes is twofold - to ensure that new and/or modified Order Management related infrastructure is deployed effectively, and to ensure that Order Management processes can operate effectively.

For the Order Management processes the role of the Support Order Management processes is to make sure that there is sufficient process capacity and capability (for example information, materials, systems and resources) so that the Order Management processes can operate effectively. Examples are information on how to process orders for specific product offerings, information needed to carry out designs, materials needed to confirm customer order requests, systems needed to validate product offering availability.

The responsibilities of these processes include, but are not limited to:

- forecasting at an operational level customer order Management volume requirements;
- the capacity planning associated with the deployment of new and/or modified customer order Management infrastructure;
- establishment and monitoring of organizational arrangements to support deployment and operation of new and/or modified customer order Management infrastructure;
- creation, deployment, modification and/or upgrading of customer order Management infrastructure deployment support tools (including Customer Inventory and Product Offer Inventory) and processes for new and/or modified customer order Management infrastructure;
- authoring, reviewing and approving operational procedures developed by Marketing andamp; Offer Management processes prior to customer order Management infrastructure deployment;
- the testing and acceptance of new and/or modified customer order Management infrastructure as part of the handover procedure from the Marketing andamp; Offer Management processes to Operations;
- detecting customer order Management infrastructure operational limitations and/or deployment incompatibilities and providing requirements to address these aspects to Marketing andamp; Offer Management processes;
- co-ordination and roll-out, in accordance with approved plans, of the approved new and/or modified customer order Management infrastructure;
- monitoring capacity utilization of deployed customer order Management infrastructure to provide early detection of potential customer order Management infrastructure shortfalls;
- reconfiguration and re-arrangement of under-utilized deployed customer order Management infrastructure;
- managing recovery and/or removal of obsolete or unviable customer order Management infrastructure;
- reporting on deployed customer order Management infrastructure capacity;
- Tracking and monitoring of the customer order Management infrastructure deployment processes and costs (including where customer order Management infrastructure is deployed and managed by third parties),
- reporting on the capability of the customer order Management infrastructure deployment processes
- establishing and managing customer order Management notification facilities and lists to support the Order Management notification and reporting processes
The processes undertake trend analysis on order Management, such as time taken to complete a customer order, frequency and type of Order Management process issues involved, and canceled orders.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Ensure Order Management Capability -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Ensure Order Management Capability">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Ensure Order Management Capability</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Ensure that there is capability (for example, information, materials, systems and resources) so that the Order Management processes can operate effectively. Examples are materials needed to confirm customer order requests and systems needed to validate product offering availability.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

