<rdfs:comment>Customer Order Processing Management business process directs and controls all activities that operationally realize orders for customer. 

Customer Order Processing Managment assures the capture, processing, fulfillment, "shipping", delivery and reporting of customer orders from feasibility assessment, purchasing, payent, fulfullment and followup with the customer for closure.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Manage Customer Order Placement -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Manage Customer Order Placement">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Manage Customer Order Placement</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Manage Customer Order Placement business activity directs and controls the capture of information to enable create customer order, change customer order and validate customer order based on ordering information from customer.

Manage Customer Order Placemet ensures that the organization can identify customers, facilitate product selection, capture requirements and confirm payments associated to orders.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Capture Customer Order -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Capture Customer Order">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Capture Customer Order</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Capture Customer Order business activity identifies all customer order requirements from the customer, including customer information, requested products/services, expected terms of delivery, and the customer order policy related to the order. 

Capture Customer Order formalizes an order in order to initiate a Customer Order Validation process.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Change Customer Order -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Change Customer Order">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Change Customer Order</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Change Customer Order business activity modifies customer orders and order items according to customer order management policies. 

Change Customer Order enables editing orders based on order details provided by the customer, including order items, quantities, terms underlying the ordering, variants of items etc.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Validate Customer Order -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Validate Customer Order">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Validate Customer Order</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Validate Customer Order business activity assures customer orders are complete with all requirements that meet the order policies as well as any related business rules and policy. 

Validate Customer Order business activity supports feasibility checks, identifying duplicate customer orders, performing customer information verification, fraud check, item validation, credit limit requirement etc. and payment confirmation.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Manage Customer Order Payment -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Manage Customer Order Payment">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Manage Customer Order Payment</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Manage Customer Order Payment business activity directs and controls customer payments for orders received. It is responsible for ensuring that customer payments for orders are processed, and accounted for correctly. 

This business activity ensures that payments are received, validated, correctly applied to the customers accounts, tracked for compliance, and where applicable the corresponding portion of the payment sent to upstream business partners.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Receive Customer Order Payment -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Receive Customer Order Payment">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Receive Customer Order Payment</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Receive Customer Order Payment business activity is responsbile for receiving payments from customers (via any medium, channel or means). 

Receive Customer Order Payment will support the organization's customer order management policies, such as customer order payment types, customer order payment modes, customer order payment plans etc.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Validate Customer Order Payment -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Validate Customer Order Payment">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Validate Customer Order Payment</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Validate Customer Order Payment business activity is responsible check that payment received is valid and approved. 

Validate Customer Order Payment will support fraud detection and preverntion policies.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Monitor Customer Order Payment -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Monitor Customer Order Payment">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Monitor Customer Order Payment</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Monitor Customer Order Payment business activity tracks payments to ensure they are processed on time and in compliance with the organizations customer order management policies.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Send Customer Order Payment -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Send Customer Order Payment">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Send Customer Order Payment</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Send Customer Order Payment business activity is responsible for transfering to upstream business partners based on the underlying terms supporting the customer order management process.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Manage Customer Order Fulfillment -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Manage Customer Order Fulfillment">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Manage Customer Order Fulfillment</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Manage Customer Order Fulfillment business activity directs and controls all activities that provision and activate orders marked for fulfillment. 

Manage Customer Order Fulfillment ensure customer orders are organized and arranged (orchestrated), and tracked to meet committed ordering terms.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Manage Customer Order Fallout -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Manage Customer Order Fallout">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Manage Customer Order Fallout</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Manage Customer Order Fallout business activity controls orders that have failed during the fullfillment stage of a customer order process. 

Manage Order Fallout identify any failed customer order, investigates fallout causes, implements resolution of fallouts, and where required may escalate fallouts based on business and customer expectations.  This process deals with managing (monitoring, identifying, assigning, and reporting) orders fallouts due to exceptions in the processing stage. This could be due to many reasons including flight time concerns (e.g. capacity, outages etc. 

These scenarios lead to the need to manage exceptions that demand interventions that are not part of the standard customer order fulfilment lifecycle. It includes assessing order fallout for root cause and identification of preventive and corrective actions.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Identify Customer Order Fallout -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Identify Customer Order Fallout">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Identify Customer Order Fallout</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Identify Customer Order Fallout business activity searches and finds customer orders that have failed the customer order process. 

Identify Customer Order Fallout can will visibility in the delivery activity of the customer order, as well as reporting of customer order fallouts.  In "Identify Customer Order Fallout" this business activity will categorize and prioritize fallout customer orders according to business rules and policies (terms of service).</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Investigate Customer Order Fallout -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Investigate Customer Order Fallout">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Investigate Customer Order Fallout</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Investigate Customer Order Fallout business activity covers tasks that assess customer orders that have failed. 

Investigate Customer Order Fallout include activities to identify the customer order fallout root cause,  evaluation and and reporting customer order fallout impact, and providing all attribution to support resolving the Customer Order Fallout.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Investigate Customer Order Fallout -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Investigate Customer Order Fallout">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Investigate Customer Order Fallout</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Investigate Customer Order Fallout business activity covers tasks that assess customer orders that have failed. 

Investigate Customer Order Fallout include activities to identify the customer order fallout root cause,  evaluation and and reporting customer order fallout impact, and providing all attribution to support resolving the Customer Order Fallout.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Resolve Customer Order Fallout -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Resolve Customer Order Fallout">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Resolve Customer Order Fallout</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Resolve Customer Order Fallout business activity find resolution to fallout customer orders, given their root cause. 

Resolve Customer Order Fallout activities may trigger interactions that provide temporary workaround solution, but is ultimately responsible to ensure resolution supports customer management objectives.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Escalate Customer Order Fallout -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Escalate Customer Order Fallout">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Escalate Customer Order Fallout</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Escalate Customer Order Fallout busiess activity logs and communicates concerns with Customer Order Fallout in a bid to effectively resolve the fallout. 

Escalate Customer Order Fallout may increase the rapid resolution of the fallout; bring more attention to the fallout impact; or prioritize allocation of capacity and capabilities to addressing the customer order fallout; by gaining higher-level support for the resolution of the fallout customer order.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Manage Customer Order Delivery -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Manage Customer Order Delivery">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Manage Customer Order Delivery</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Manage Customer Order Delivery business activity directs and controls activities that deliver orders according to the requirement of the customer.

Manage Customer Order Delivery</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Plan Customer Order Delivery -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Plan Customer Order Delivery">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Plan Customer Order Delivery</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Plan Customer Order Delivery business activity defines the required customer order delivery activities, customer order delivery support requirements and the schedule to follow in fulfulling the customer order. 

Plan Customer Order Delivery business activity includes all tasks for the customer order delivery, including identifying the supporting activities,  scheduling the activities, relating them together based on customer orderig procedures and guidelines.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Deliver Customer Order -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Deliver Customer Order">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Deliver Customer Order</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Deliver Customer Order business actiity directs and controls the actity of providing the ready items of the customer rorder to the customer.  

Delivery Customer Order business activity identfies the customer to be delivered to, confirms all items related to the order, and follow the Plan Customer Order delivery plan to deliver the order.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Monitor Customer Order Delivery -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Monitor Customer Order Delivery">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Monitor Customer Order Delivery</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Monitor Customer Order Delivery business activity checks and tracks customer order delivery activities with status reporting. 

Monitor Customer Order Delivery business activity ensures orders are tracks with their statuses across the order fulfillment lifecycle.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Verify Customer Order Delivery -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Verify Customer Order Delivery">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Verify Customer Order Delivery</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Verify Custoemr Order Delivery business activity checks the validity of the order delivery status according to the Customer Order. 

Verify Customer Order Delivery ensures that all supporting delivery requirements and obligations of the customer order has been completely fulfilled to the customer.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Manage Customer Order Cancellation -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Manage Customer Order Cancellation">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Manage Customer Order Cancellation</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Manage Customer Order Cancellation business activity directs and controls the review, acceptance and processing of order cancellation requests in accordance to the order management policies and procedures. 

Manage Customer Order Cancellation includes activities that enable review cancellation requests, approve or reject cancellation requests, and overseas any returns applicable to the review outcome of cancellation requests.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Manage Customer Order Cancellation Request -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Manage Customer Order Cancellation Request">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Manage Customer Order Cancellation Request</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Manage Customer Order Cancellation Request business activity controls activities that enable assess customer order cancellation requests and any related impact to the busines and customer. 

Manage Customer Order Cancellation Request  requires a Customer Order to have been accepted and includes negotiations with customer, mediation of cancellation reasons and effectively processing a request for onward action.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Manage Customer Order Cancellation Return -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Manage Customer Order Cancellation Return">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Manage Customer Order Cancellation Return</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Manage Customer Order Cancellation Return business activity controls activities that direct any returns associated to successfully accepted customer order cancellation request.

Manage Customer Order Cancellation Return will assure all financial and non-financial implications for the cancelled customer order do net off based on both the allocated effort from the organization's side, as well as the impact on future customer management concerns.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Manage Customer Order Completion -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Manage Customer Order Completion">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Manage Customer Order Completion</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Manage Customer Order Completion business activity controls activities to confirm that an order has been successfully delivered/shipped to the customer. 

Manage Customer Order Completion includes activities that assure delivery/shipment is successfully processed by the business, and there is a confirmation that the customrer order is in effectively in a delivery/shipping state.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Manage Customer Order Management Report -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Manage Customer Order Management Report">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Manage Customer Order Management Report</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Manage Customer Order Management Report buisiness activity provides detailed account of Customer Order Management activities, representing state and status of customer orders across the customer order lifecycle. 

Manage Customer Order Management Report provides monitoring, tracking and customer order status updates/notification as needed to all stakeholders linked to the customer ordering and fulfillment activities.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Manage Customer Order Closure -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Manage Customer Order Closure">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Manage Customer Order Closure</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Manage Customer Order Closure business actuvity ensures that customer has confirmed the delivery of a completed customer order. 

Manage Customer Order Closure business activity closes-the-loop of between the Customer Order Completion process and the confirmation by the Customer. This business activity includes tasks to communicate and confirm delivery to customer; cancellation of any open line items in the customer order; and reports the customer order completion to related stakeholders.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Manage Customer Order Policy -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Manage Customer Order Policy">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Manage Customer Order Policy</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Manage Customer Order Policy business process controls all business and technical procedures that support customer order scenarios and activities.

Manage Customer Order Policy ensures customer order will be processed in a manner that is efficient and accurate based on implied levels of business agreement with customers.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Define Customer Order Policy -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Define Customer Order Policy">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Define Customer Order Policy</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Define Customer Order Policy business activity develops and establish the procedures, guidelines and practices that guide customer order management scenarios and activities.

Define Customer Order Policy supports the lifecycle of an Order from a Customer by establishing the procedures and guidelines (including obligations of both the customer and the organization) for decisions taken while processing customer orders. These policy govern the order processing lifecycle.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Implement Customer Order Policy -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Implement Customer Order Policy">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Implement Customer Order Policy</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Implement Customer Order Policy business activity administer and enforces the guidelines and practices that support the realization of customer orders.

Implement Customer Order Policy includes tasks that achieve the goals and objectives establshed for Customer Management, including communication, publication and educating the existence of the customer order policies.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Change Customer Order Policy -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Change Customer Order Policy">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Change Customer Order Policy</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Change Customer Order Policy business activity amends and remodels customer order guidelines and practices in support of the organization's customer management objectives. 

Change Customer Order Policy ensures that changes to customer order policies are done with all concerned parties included in the decision to change a policy. This includes the impact on customer management process, impact on the customer, and all associated "Customer Order Policy" stakeholders.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Track and Manage Customer Order Handling (Deleted) -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Track and Manage Customer Order Handling (Deleted)">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Track and Manage Customer Order Handling (Deleted)</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Not used for this process element</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Customer Relationship Management -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Customer Relationship Management">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Customer Relationship Management</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>The purpose of this process is to manage the relationship of the Customer and the enterprise. This process may be triggered at very early stages of the customer lifecycle (for example, for leads and prospects which are potential customers) and until the termination of the customer relationship between the enterprise and the customer. This processes is in charge of managing the customer relationship with the enterprise and of the customer profile. This process ensure that each customer gets a unique identity and that customer identities are not duplicated in the enterprise. This process is also in charge of evaluating the customer value, the customer risk (credit risk, fraud risk, influence risk, and churn risk) of validating the customer satisfaction. 
The customer data is managed by the Customer Information Management process.
Was previously named Customer Relationship Management.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Customer Relationship Management -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Customer Relationship Management">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Customer Relationship Management</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>The purpose of this process is to manage the relationship of the Customer and the enterprise. This process may be triggered at very early stages of the customer lifecycle (for example, for leads and prospects which are potential customers) and until the termination of the customer relationship between the enterprise and the customer. This processes is in charge of managing the customer relationship with the enterprise and of the customer profile. This process ensure that each customer gets a unique identity and that customer identities are not duplicated in the enterprise. This process is also in charge of evaluating the customer value, the customer risk (credit risk, fraud risk, influence risk, and churn risk) of validating the customer satisfaction. 
The customer data is managed by the Customer Information Management process.
Was previously named Customer Relationship Management.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Customer Relationship Management -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Customer Relationship Management">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Customer Relationship Management</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>The purpose of this process is to manage the relationship of the Customer and the enterprise. This process may be triggered at very early stages of the customer lifecycle (for example, for leads and prospects which are potential customers) and until the termination of the customer relationship between the enterprise and the customer. This processes is in charge of managing the customer relationship with the enterprise and of the customer profile. This process ensure that each customer gets a unique identity and that customer identities are not duplicated in the enterprise. This process is also in charge of evaluating the customer value, the customer risk (credit risk, fraud risk, influence risk, and churn risk) of validating the customer satisfaction. 
The customer data is managed by the Customer Information Management process.
Was previously named Customer Relationship Management.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Enable Retention and Loyalty -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Enable Retention and Loyalty">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Enable Retention and Loyalty</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Retention and Loyalty processes deal with all functionalities related to the retention of acquired customers, and the use of loyalty schemes in the potential acquisition of customers. They establish a complete understanding of the needs of the customer, a determination of the value of the customer to the enterprise, determination of opportunities and risks for specific customers, etc. These processes collect and analyze data from all enterprise and customer contact.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

