<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Manage Architecture Skillsets">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Manage Architecture Skillsets</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Not used for this process element.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Provide Reference Source for Standard Operating Environment -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Provide Reference Source for Standard Operating Environment">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Provide Reference Source for Standard Operating Environment</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Provides the reference source for the enterprise Standard Operating Environment that is the collection of applications, hardware, software and network components that have been standardized for use across the enterprise. The business strategies and plans provide a key starting point for the development and direction provided. Note that enterprise architecture management covers both IT and network technologies, and the processes impact other areas within the eTOM model, such as Knowledge Management and Process Architecture Management.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Co-ordinate Architecture Review -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Co-ordinate Architecture Review">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Co-ordinate Architecture Review</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Not used for this process element.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Manage Group Enterprise -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Manage Group Enterprise">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Manage Group Enterprise</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Manage Group Enterprise business activity plans, directs and coordinates strategy and enterprise planning across the organizations  business units, as well as between the enterprise and its subsidiaries.

Manage Group Enterprise business activity includes planning and implementation of cross-business unit operations, harmonization of processes and communication systems; funding and cross-subsidies, investment for business development planning, execution and management of existing and new business activities.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Plan and Implement Cross-Business Unit Operation -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Plan and Implement Cross-Business Unit Operation">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Plan and Implement Cross-Business Unit Operation</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Planning and implementation of cross-business unit operation. These processes are responsible for planning and management of coordination across business units within the enterprise, and between the enterprise and its subsidiaries (note that similar interactions concerning outsourcing involving other parties is handled elsewhere, through processes located in the Engaged Party Domain). The focus is on processes concerned with the co-ordination within the enterprises own organization, including subsidiaries, from an Enterprise-wide point of view.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Harmonize Processes and Communication Systems across Business Units -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Harmonize Processes and Communication Systems across Business Units">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Harmonize Processes and Communication Systems across Business Units</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Not used for this process element.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Manage Funding and Cross-Subsidies across Business Units -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Manage Funding and Cross-Subsidies across Business Units">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Manage Funding and Cross-Subsidies across Business Units</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Not used for this process element.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Manage Investment for Business Development -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Manage Investment for Business Development">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Manage Investment for Business Development</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Not used for this process element.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Co-ordinate Business Activities -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Co-ordinate Business Activities">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Co-ordinate Business Activities</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Not used for this process element.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Manage Enterprise Capacity -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Manage Enterprise Capacity">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Manage Enterprise Capacity</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Enterprise Capacity Management business process establishes current and future enterprise "resources" (i.e. materials, staff, stock, supplies etc.) are sufficient to meet planned and forecasted business needs.
Enterprise Capacity Management business process support the organization in determining optimal availability for current and future business intents for use or consumption, and aligns the allocation of available and planned "resources" relationship between all value streams, such product management, service management and production resource management. Through this business process, maximum levels of output that an organization can sustain for production (to make a product or provide a service) are defined and managed in a continuum.
Enterprise Capacity Management process works closely with service level management to ensure that the business requirements for capacity are meet expectations of the enterprises performance goals. Enterprise Capacity Management also serves as a focal point for any capacity issues in the organization as it supports product, services and resources planning, availability and performance.
Examples of Enterprise Capacity Management include:
A telco that can support 200 million minutes of use across a 200 solar powered base stations with a 40 man network operations team and 1000 subscribers in a week.
A cafand#233; that can brew 1800 cups of coffee in a working day of 8 hours.
A call center scoped to field 7,000 calls per week with 120 agents in a 3 shift cycle.
An automobile production line that can assemble 250 trucks per month across 3 truck models.
A restaurant that is designed to support seating capacity that accommodates a maximum of 100 diners at its peak time per week.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Enterprise Capacity Planning -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Enterprise Capacity Planning">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Enterprise Capacity Planning</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Enterprise Capacity Planning business process activity handle the tasks of balancing available "resources" against value streams need in order to meet the enterprises' demand management program.
Enterprise Capacity Planning maintains a holistic view across the enterprise to ensure a match of supply with demand given all the resources available to the enterprise. It receives reports from all value streams (product/service and resource), and supports the overarching capacity management policies.
Enterprise Capacity Planning impacts on all the enterprise, it's projects, and measures and tracks the allocation and use of capacity based on well defined capacity management strategy.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Enterprise Capacity Management Requirement -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Enterprise Capacity Management Requirement">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Enterprise Capacity Management Requirement</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Enterprise Capacity Management Requirement business activity help to identify and deal with the Enterprises demand program to support any and all of the value streams, including products, service and resources altogether.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Manage Enterprise Catalog Strategy -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Manage Enterprise Catalog Strategy">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Manage Enterprise Catalog Strategy</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Manage Enterprise Catalog Strategy business activity directs and controls the definition of the overarching Catalog Management strategy for the organization. 

Manage Enterprise Catalog Strategy business activity include activities to oversee all Catalog Management in the organization and with its subsidiaries, Catalog Management Integration and Catalog Management implementation between and across functions and operating subsidiaries.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Manage Enterprise Catalog Management Policy -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Manage Enterprise Catalog Management Policy">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Manage Enterprise Catalog Management Policy</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Not used for this process element.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Manage Enterprise Catalog Management Standard -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Manage Enterprise Catalog Management Standard">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Manage Enterprise Catalog Management Standard</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Manage Enterprise Catalog Management Standard activity identify and promulgate rules and references for managing conformity of Catalogs for information integrity across the enterprises catalogs.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Enterprise Audit and Risk Management -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Enterprise Audit and Risk Management">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Enterprise Audit and Risk Management</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Enterprise Audit and Risk Management business process directs and controls activities that assess the enterprises compliance and consistency in performance of activities against regulations and internal policies, and  as well manage the understanding and addressing of enterprise business risks. 
Enterprise Audit and Risk Management address needs of all enterprise business functions and activities with enterprise audit management and enterprise risk management.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Manage Enterprise Audit -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Manage Enterprise Audit">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Manage Enterprise Audit</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Manage Enterprise Audit business activity directs and controls the assessment, evaluation and reporting on the enterprises state of compliance,  according to regulations and internal policies, by way of its day-to-day of activities while checking and reporting consistency operating against established directives.  

Manage Enterprise Audit helps simplify and well-organize the workflow and collaboration process of compiling and reporting of audits and their findings. The business activity provide assurance to senior management and the enterprise Board that the business processes and controls are effective and conform to relevant directives and applicable standards.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Define Audit Policy -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Define Audit Policy">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Define Audit Policy</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Defines the audit policies and procedures. It will depend on the type of audit like but not limited to Risk audit, Data Management, Data Governance Audit etc.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Define Audit Mechanism -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Define Audit Mechanism">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Define Audit Mechanism</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Define the audit approach to be used depending on the circumstances, as well as the assessment methodology and scoring approach to be used. identify, prioritize and manage audit program .</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Assess Operational Activities -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Assess Operational Activities">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Assess Operational Activities</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Assess operational activities to ensure necessary or mandated control structures are in place.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Evaluate Operational Activities -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Evaluate Operational Activities">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Evaluate Operational Activities</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Provide an estimate to the extent to which the procedures are followed and are effective.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Report Audits -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Report Audits">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Report Audits</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Provide assurance to senior management and the enterprise Board that the enterprise operational processes and controls are effective and conform to relevant adopted standards (which may be externally imposed or internally adopted). Audit Management processes may be managed by external independent organizations, or by internal groups within the enterprise, but in either case are designed to support senior management/Board assurance. However, the assurance role of the processes is more related to reactive assessment. The processes ensure that appropriate reports relating to compliance and capability are provided to senior management/Board within appropriate defined timeframes.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Apply Audit Mechanisms Proactively -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Apply Audit Mechanisms Proactively">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Apply Audit Mechanisms Proactively</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Use audit mechanisms proactively to develop assessment methodologies, scoring systems, and advice to operational groups who are responsible for the operations processes.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Enterprise Risk Management -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Enterprise Risk Management">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Enterprise Risk Management</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Enterprise Risk Management business activity directs and controls the understanding, analyzing and addressing of situations that are probable, or expose the enterprise to all threats.

Enterprise Risk Management includes activities that implement mediatory actions, such as insurance, business continuity, health and safety, corporate governance, engineering, planning and financial services.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Business Continuity Management -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Business Continuity Management">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Business Continuity Management</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Business Continuity Management processes manage the development of strategies, policies, plans, organizational roles and responsibilities, and escalation procedures for ensuring continuation of business processes and activities in the event of serious and/or sustained interruption. These processes ensure that appropriate plans and procedures are established and tested to provide continuous operation, or controlled re-establishment, of key business processes and activities, to provide for a controlled recovery of infrastructure capability to normal levels, and for determination of operational accountability and processes until the abnormal circumstances are resolved. These processes have four major aspects:
- Business continuity planning which provides for the proactive planning and testing of business and operational procedure continuity;
- Infrastructure recovery planning which provides for the pro-active determination of recovery and backup procedures for all key infrastructure capabilities, and their proactive testing;
- Serious incident management planning which defines the operational roles and responsibilities, and proactively defines the operational procedures and escalation criteria which are initiated when abnormal operation circumstances occur
- Business continuity management methodologies, which ensure consistent application of business continuity management across the enterprise.
Note that business continuity management is an extended process structure which incorporates disaster recovery planning.
Note that serious incident management is used instead of crisis management as serious disruption can occur to the business through events which would not normally be classified as a crisis.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Co-ordinate Business Continuity -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Co-ordinate Business Continuity">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Co-ordinate Business Continuity</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Manage the development of strategies, policies, plans, organizational roles and responsibilities, and escalation procedures for ensuring continuation of business processes and activities in the event of serious and/or sustained interruption. These processes ensure that appropriate plans and procedures are established and tested to provide continuous operation, or controlled re-establishment, of key business processes and activities, to provide for a controlled recovery of infrastructure capability to normal levels, and for determination of operational accountability and processes until the abnormal circumstances are resolved.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Plan Business Continuity -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Plan Business Continuity">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Plan Business Continuity</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Not used for this process element.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Plan Infrastructure Recovery -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Plan Infrastructure Recovery">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Plan Infrastructure Recovery</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Not used for this process element.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Plan Serious Incident Management -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Plan Serious Incident Management">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Plan Serious Incident Management</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Serious incident management planning which defines the operational roles and responsibilities, and proactively defines the operational procedures and escalation criteria which are initiated when abnormal operation circumstances occur. Note that serious incident management is used instead of crisis management as serious disruption can occur to the business through events which would not normally be classified as a crisis.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Manage Business Continuity Methodologies -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Manage Business Continuity Methodologies">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Manage Business Continuity Methodologies</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Business continuity management methodologies, which ensure consistent application of business continuity management across the enterprise. Note that business continuity management is an extended process structure which incorporates disaster recovery planning</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Insurance Management -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Insurance Management">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Insurance Management</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Insurance Management processes are responsible for assessing and managing the insurable risks within an enterprise. These processes identify areas and activities within the enterprise where risk aspects are insurable, and analyze the cost/benefits of undertaking specific insurance. These processes provide advice and consultancy to the enterprise relating to insurance of local activities and programs. These processes manage the engagement with the external insurance industry, and administer insurance policies and portfolios. Depending on the nature of the risk being insured, the  Party Offering Development and Retirement processes are used to select an appropriate insurer, in other cases where the number of insurance providers is small, the negotiation process may be directly managed by these processes.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Identify Insurable Risks -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Identify Insurable Risks">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Identify Insurable Risks</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Not used for this process element.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Analyze Insurance Cost/Benefits -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Analyze Insurance Cost/Benefits">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Analyze Insurance Cost/Benefits</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Not used for this process element.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Provide Insurance Advice -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Provide Insurance Advice">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Provide Insurance Advice</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Not used for this process element.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Manage Insurance Portfolio -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Manage Insurance Portfolio">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Manage Insurance Portfolio</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Manage the engagement with the external insurance industry, and administer insurance policies and portfolios. Depending on the nature of the risk being insured, the  Party Offering Development and Retirement processes are used to select an appropriate insurer, in other cases where the number of insurance providers is small, the negotiation process may be directly managed by these processes.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Knowledge Management -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Knowledge Management">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Knowledge Management</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Knowledge Management business activity manage the establishment, assessment, operations and evaluation of processes and capabilities that support knowledge capture, knowledge organization, knowledge operations and knowledge evaluation across the enterprise. Knowledge Management processes support the organization across a gamut of key activities including protecting its intellectual properties, business resilience and as well manages the standards for creating and managing information and information capture and stored, assigned, and distributed. Knowledge in the enterprise includes both the tacit and explicit knowledge contained with the enterprise.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Assess Knowledge Management Needs -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Assess Knowledge Management Needs">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Assess Knowledge Management Needs</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Assess Knowledge Management needs business activity analyzes to understand the knowledge needs of enterprise functions, translated the business needs into knowledge management targets and identify knowledge management activities to address the needs. Assess Knowledge Management Needs ensures that assessment of the process and capabilities for knowledge management capture current state of knowledge management activities across enterprise functions. The assessment process solicits input from enterprise functions and 'Evaluate Knowledge Management Performance' to identify improvements for knowledge management.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Establish Knowledge Management -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Establish Knowledge Management">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Establish Knowledge Management</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Establish Knowledge Management business activity sets up the processes and capabilities that are required to institutionalize and operationalize knowledge management activities across all the enterprise.  Establish Knowledge Management business activity leverage the strategic Initiative of the enterprise as an input to make knowledge management support the business goals. It includes defining 'knowledge management lifecycle' and 'implementing knowledge management capabilities'.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Define Knowledge Management lifecycle -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Define Knowledge Management lifecycle">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Define Knowledge Management lifecycle</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Define Knowledge Management Lifecycle business activity is responsible for describing all the stages that support knowledge management across the enterprise. Define Knowledge Management Lifecycle defines 'who', 'what', 'when', 'where' and 'how' of activities that support institutionalizing and operationalizing knowledge management. This includes description of expectation for the creation, sharing, auditing, organizing and storage of knowledge in support of the enterprises business goals.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Implement Knowledge Management capability -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Implement Knowledge Management capability">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Implement Knowledge Management capability</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Implement Knowledge Management Capability business activity puts into effect the required capabilities (processes, people and technology) that support operationalizing knowledge management activities.  Implement Knowledge Management Capability covers the processes and mechanisms that support the acquisition to dissemination of  knowledge within the enterprises business functions, and with stakeholders.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Operate Knowledge Management -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Operate Knowledge Management">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Operate Knowledge Management</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Operate Knowledge Management business activity controls and administers day-to-day tasks that support knowledge acquisition, knowledge organization, knowledge refinement, knowledge storage, knowledge distribution and knowledge application. Operate Knowledge Management supports enterprise business functions to identify knowledge objects, run different knowledge operation models, and address their knowledge handling goals.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Acquire Knowledge -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Acquire Knowledge">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Acquire Knowledge</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Acquire Knowledge business activity handles gathering or collecting knowledge from various sources, including discovering knowledge based on value it brings to the organization.  This business activity adds new knowledge to a knowledge base and support 'Refine Knowledge', 'Distribute Knowledge' and 'Apply Knowledge'.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Organize Knowledge -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Organize Knowledge">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Organize Knowledge</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Organize Knowledge business activity handles the classification, mapping, indexing, and categorization of knowledge to support activities that acquire, store and retrieve knowledge.  The enterprise needs to make  connections between different knowledge objects. With connections from knowledge objects, the enterprise structures knowledge in a way that accurately and meaningfully organizes knowledge for refinement, storage, distribution and application.  Organize Knowledge uses "systems" and processes to generate, transform, manage, use, and transfer knowledge-based products and services to achieve enterprise business goals and objectives.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Refine Knowledge -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Refine Knowledge">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Refine Knowledge</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Refine Knowledge business activity handles the evaluation, analysis and optimization of knowledge to be stored by the enterprise. Refine Knowledge enables the enterprise to iteratively improve its knowledge operations activities in an effort to improve the quality of the enterprises knowledge objects.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Store Knowledge -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Store Knowledge">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Store Knowledge</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Store Knowledge business activity handles the storage of knowledge objects to support the enterprises knowledge management goals.  Store knowledge ensures the organization can formally account for knowledge it in its possession through well-defined storage medium/media.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Distribute Knowledge -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Distribute Knowledge">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Distribute Knowledge</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Distribute Knowledge business activity handles tasks that assign and share knowledge among enterprise business functions through various defined techniques, people, and technologies.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Evaluate Knowledge Management Performance -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Evaluate Knowledge Management Performance">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Evaluate Knowledge Management Performance</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Evaluate Knowledge Management Performance business activity assesses performance of knowledge management outcomes based on how knowledge management lifecycle and knowledge management operations support the achievement of business goals.  Evaluate Knowledge Management Performance supports 'assess knowledge management needs', 'establish knowledge management', and 'knowledge management operations' by preventing repeated missteps, guiding development, and sharing of knowledge to give the enterprise and its business functions a competitive edge.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Financial Management -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Financial Management">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Financial Management</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Financial Management processes manage the financial aspects of the enterprise such as Treasury, Banking, Payroll, Financial Planning and Accounting Operations functions, e.g., Accounts Receivable and Payable. These processes are accountable for the financial health of the enterprise, managing cash flow, etc.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Define Financial Management Approach -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Define Financial Management Approach">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Define Financial Management Approach</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>This process ensures that the program leadership has explicitly defined the financial controls
and processes for the program, including financial management and the program financial reporting. Obtain approval of the program financial management Approach from key stakeholders, including the sponsoring organization finance entity.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

