<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Notify Legal Environment Changes">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Notify Legal Environment Changes</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Not used for this process element.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Manage Legal Actions -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Manage Legal Actions">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Manage Legal Actions</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Not used for this process element.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Board and Shares/Securities Management -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Board and Shares/Securities Management">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Board and Shares/Securities Management</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>The Board and Shares/Securities Management processes manage all activities associated with Board administration and securities regulation. The Board Management processes manage Board related activities, and communication of Board decisions throughout the enterprise as required. Shares/Securities Management manages all activities associated with securities/shares of the enterprise and any securities/company regulations impacting on the company, including the administration and management of continuous disclosure/announcements to the securities exchange and/or securities/company regulator. These processes manage all activities associated with modifying the capital/equity structure of the enterprise, including all logistics functions associated with approaching the market for capital/increased equity. These processes manage and administer the enterprises share/stock registry.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Manage Board Related Activities -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Manage Board Related Activities">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Manage Board Related Activities</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Not used for this process element.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Manage Shares/Securities -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Manage Shares/Securities">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Manage Shares/Securities</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Manage activities associated with securities/shares of the enterprise and any securities/company regulations impacting on the company, including the administration and management of continuous disclosure/announcements to the securities exchange and/or securities/company regulator.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Manage Capital/Equity Activities -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Manage Capital/Equity Activities">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Manage Capital/Equity Activities</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Not used for this process element.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Manage Share/Stock Registry -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Manage Share/Stock Registry">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Manage Share/Stock Registry</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Not used for this process element.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Manage Transparency -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Manage Transparency">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Manage Transparency</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Manage Transparency business activity is in charge of enabling open communication and assuring free flow of information and data within the enterprise, and with customers, business partners and all other stakeholders.

Manage Transparency business activity include tasks to Establish Trust and Manage Disclosure of information and data. This is in order to foster the belief in the accuracy, reliability and timely exchanges between the enterprise and customers, business partners, employees and other stakeholders.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Establish Trust -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Establish Trust">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Establish Trust</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Establish Trust business activity sets up an environment in the enterprise that foster positive relationships, good judgement with expertise, and maintaining consistency in exchanges across all interactions and experiences.

Establish Trust business activity supports the enterprise to Manage Transparency by facilitating consistent and open exchanges with customers, business partners, employees and all other stakeholders.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Manage Disclosure -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Manage Disclosure">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Manage Disclosure</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Manage Disclosure business activity is in charge of directing and controlling the release and publication of facts or information known customers, business partners, employees and other stakeholders (such as investors). 

Manage Disclosure business activity includes tasks that consolidate data and information,  maintains repository of documents and reports required for statutory reporting (e.g. regulatory filings). Manage Disclosure by enterprises makes customers, investors, and stakeholders involved in doing business with the company aware of pertinent information.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Manage Standards -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Manage Standards">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Manage Standards</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Manage Standards business activity is in charge of controlling and directing all activities that support creating protocols that guide the enterprise in creating, applying and using products and services based on the consensus of all the relevant parties in the industry.

Manage Standards business activity ensures the safety, interoperability, and compatibility of products and services used by the enterprise and with partners (traditional or ecosystem partners).</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Define Standardization Requirement -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Define Standardization Requirement">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Define Standardization Requirement</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Define Standardization Requirement
Manage Standardization Requirement business activity states and describes the needs that must support the development of standards across the enterprise. 

Manage Standardization Requirement supports the Manage Standards business activity by ensuring that there exists the steps and check points that assure there is consensus underpinning the establishment, documenting, analyzing, tracing, prioritizing and agreeing on requirements for standards.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Establish Best Practice Model -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Establish Best Practice Model">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Establish Best Practice Model</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Establish Best Practices Model business activity sets up the generally accepted ideas or methods that are considered superior and documents them along with the results they produce.

Establish Best Practice Model business activities include tasks that describe the representational view or framework that embody the practice and proven solutions that help to address a problem or goals for the best practice. The value behind establishing these best practices model is to identify methods that are confirmed as effective, and reduce the need to 'reinvent the wheel'.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Legitimize Standard -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Legitimize Standard">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Legitimize Standard</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Legitimize Standard business activity is in charge of approve and allowing a standard to be formally accepted by the enterprise and its business functions.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Systematize Standards Use -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Systematize Standards Use">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Systematize Standards Use</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Systematize Standards Use business activity is  in charge of applying, evaluating and managing the lifecycle of standards formally recognized by the enterprise.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Manage Integrity -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Manage Integrity">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Manage Integrity</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Manage Integrity business activity is in charge maintaining the highest ethical standards in every aspect of enterprises' business. 

Manage Integrity tasks include assessing integrity, responding to integrity assessment, managing ethics, and managing the enterprises'' reputation. This business activity will leverage Risk Management in supporting the enterprise governance objectives. 

Manage Integrity will provide ongoing and systematized processes to guide behaviors which assure integrity of people, processes and products in the enterprise, and with partners. Code Of Conduct (COC) is one of the fundamental artefacts managed by this business activity.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Remediate Integrity Assessment -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Remediate Integrity Assessment">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Remediate Integrity Assessment</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Remediate Integrity Assessment business activity is in charge of responding to findings from the enterprises integrity assessment.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Assess Integrity -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Assess Integrity">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Assess Integrity</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Assess Integrity business activity is in charge of defining assessment criteria, selecting assessment measures, designing assessment plans, collecting assessment results and interpreting integrity assessment results.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Manage Ethics -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Manage Ethics">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Manage Ethics</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Manage Ethics business activity is in charge of creating, directing and controlling how actions of all internal enterprise stakeholder follow moral values or principles established by the enterprise. 

This business activity is in charge of directing, as well as control enterprise tasks and outcomes that focus on meeting well-defined moral values or principles created. Manage Ethics is a key business activity to support Manage Integrity.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Manage Reputation -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Manage Reputation">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Manage Reputation</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Manage Reputation business activity is in charge of directing and controlling the influence and perception of the enterprise brand.

Manage Reputation business activity includes activities that responding to customer, business partner, employee and all other stakeholder feedback, monitoring enterprise reputation, addressing any content or feedback (from employees, customers, business partners and external parties) that can damage the brand.  Manage Reputation is a key business activity to support Manage Integrity.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Learning Management -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Learning Management">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Learning Management</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Learning Management business process manage activities that support building skills that can be applied to a variety of context. Learning Management business process have outcome that results in absorbing information in order to increase skills and abilities and make use of it under a variety of contexts. In contrast to training management, which focuses on the (organization) way to impact information and knowledge to instruct a trainee, learning management is about the persona involved.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Assess Learning Needs -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Assess Learning Needs">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Assess Learning Needs</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Assess Learning Needs business activity analyze and evaluate participants learning needs to identify what participants have learned, how well and where there was struggle.   Assess Learning Needs is a key activity in the learning lifecycle management. Learning Need is the gap between the learner's current level of knowledge and skills, and the level of knowledge and skills required to perform a task or a set of tasks. Assess Learning Needs helps to determine target, examine learning goals, and determine learning resources.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Define Learning Objectives -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Define Learning Objectives">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Define Learning Objectives</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Define Learning Objectives business activity establishes the overall purpose or goal from participating in a learning activity.  Define Learning Objectives establish outcomes that capture specifically what knowledge, skills, attitudes a learning program should be able to exhibit following instruction. Define Learning Objectives include defining desired outcomes (performance, conditions, and criteria), and 'define learning resources'.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Define Desired Outcomes -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Define Desired Outcomes">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Define Desired Outcomes</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Define Desired Outcomes business activity support 'Define Learning Objectives; by establishing the specific performance statement to describe the results after a learning cycle.  Define Desired Outcomes business activity establish performance conditions and criteria that describe what the learner will know or be able to do in specific, measurable terms.  Example of a Learning Objective is "Be able to felicitate customer requirements correctly."</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Build Learning Resources -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Build Learning Resources">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Build Learning Resources</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Build Learning Resources business activity establishes the learning materials or resources that instructors may use to carry out instruction and facilitate the achievement of learning goals.  Build Learning Resources ensures clear learning topics, learning resource content, develops learning concepts, and defines learning plans required to meet learning modes.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Identify Learning Topics -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Identify Learning Topics">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Identify Learning Topics</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Identify Learning Topics business activity discover relevant to support a learning objective based on the learners needs assessment outcome.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Acquire Learning Resource Content -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Acquire Learning Resource Content">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Acquire Learning Resource Content</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Acquire Learning Resource Content business activity obtain content relevant to establish curriculum for a Learning Topic.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Acquire Learning Resource Content -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Acquire Learning Resource Content">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Acquire Learning Resource Content</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Acquire Learning Resource Content business activity obtain content relevant to establish curriculum for a Learning Topic.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Develop Learning Concepts -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Develop Learning Concepts">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Develop Learning Concepts</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Develop Learning Concepts business activity establish and evolve ideas that promote successful learning resource delivery.  This business activity support Training Management by providing methods for training in order to get learners to think about the 'how' and 'why' of learning.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Develop Learning Program -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Develop Learning Program">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Develop Learning Program</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Develop Learning Program business activity establish the overall initiative and scheme to deliver a learning experience required to achieve competence.  Develop Learning Program models and develops the overall learning program to provide trainers/assessors with details about the objectives of learning and assessment; the vocational knowledge, skills or competency that learners are supported to achieve according to an overall program; a profile of the learners and their needs; and suggestions for assessment methods.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Model Learning Program -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Model Learning Program">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Model Learning Program</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Model Learning Program business activity establish a cohesive and integrated learning process for learners with input from defined learning outcome.  Model Learning Program use learning outcomes or the learning objectives (derived from the competency standards or other criteria) and outline the content, sequence and structure of learning and the delivery and assessment method/s to be used.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Develop Learning Plan -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Develop Learning Plan">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Develop Learning Plan</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Develop Learning Plan establishes a the activity schedule that defines how to achieve desired outcomes for a learning objective.  Develop Learning Plan ensures clarity so that the progress is orderly and efficient.  It includes steps to leverage learning goals as input to identify how individual learning plans may achieve one or several learning goals/objectives. It includes conducting learner assessment, applying learning styles, and when to initiate learning activities to support the goals.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Implement Learning Program -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Implement Learning Program">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Implement Learning Program</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Implement Learning Program business activity instantiates all the related learning plans and coordinates them under an integrated initiative to support achieving the learning program's experience objective.  Implement Learning Program implements the individual units of competency and provides the detailed plans for learners to achieve the specified learning outcomes.  'Learning Program' provide 'Training Management' with input for 'Evaluate Training Program'.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Evaluate Learning Program -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Evaluate Learning Program">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Evaluate Learning Program</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Evaluate Learning Program business activity assess performance of the Learning Program against overall learning objectives.  Evaluating Learning Program is an ongoing activity that starts with assessing learning program performance needs (collecting learner feedback through performance assessments, and continues to support building learning resources (e.g. designing curricula and learning experiences, facilitating Learning etc.).</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Collect Learner Feedback -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Collect Learner Feedback">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Collect Learner Feedback</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Collect Learner Feedback business activity supports 'Evaluate Learning Program' by managing activities that result in receiving information from learners about the learning program.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Assess Learning Performance -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Assess Learning Performance">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Assess Learning Performance</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Assess Learning Performance business activity analyzes the  learning activities that support a learning program to evaluate levels of understanding of curriculum and content used in learning programs.  Assess Learning Performance helps to acquire learning performance information from both the learning program, and individual learning plans using any or both of direct and indirect approach.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Training Management -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Training Management">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Training Management</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Training Management business process manage activities that instruct and deliver matters of technical knowledge according to learning management goals.  Training Management ensures the most effective approach and capability is available to transmit knowledge or information. Training Management is core to the organization being able to match capability and capacity to provide impactful means to the organizations knowledge management goals. The practice of Training Management includes directing and organizing all the training activities for the organization, including assessing training needs, designing the training, implementing the training (such as scheduling and timing the instruction activities, handling training logistics) and evaluating training outcomes against needs.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Assess Training Needs -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Assess Training Needs">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Assess Training Needs</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Assess Training Needs business activity evaluates training gaps and needs, sets training objectives, evaluates roles, prepares plans and identifies place, people, process and technology capacity required to conduct and achieve a specified training objective. Assess Training Needs lays the necessary groundwork for determining the enterprises  needs and how participants in the training will best receive the required training. Assess Training Needs captures skills proficiency of participants, frequency of skill usage and level of participants skill value to performance. Output of an Assess Training Need business activity include a map of participant (who) and type of training approach that will be most impactful (how, what, when).</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Design Training Program -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Design Training Program">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Design Training Program</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Design Training Program business activity develops the blueprint of capabilities and facilities that achieve training performance goals based on the enterprises learning objectives and knowledge management goals.  Design Training Program correlates Learning Management objectives and prior Training Management lessons into training strategies most appropriate for participants. It includes designing the Training Objectives, Developing Training Plan and identifying the type/way/method to implement training (supervised: hands-on; unsupervised: simulation, experiential etc.) that is appropriate and impactful to participants.   The output of Design Training activity eradicates the gaps in training and with capability and facilities that assure better training performance.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Define Training Objectives -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Define Training Objectives">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Define Training Objectives</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Define Training Objectives business activity establishes the training program's capabilities and facility have set objectives that enable develop successful training program.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Develop Training Implementation Method -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Develop Training Implementation Method">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Develop Training Implementation Method</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Develop Training Implementation Method business activity generate the details that support executing the training plan's chosen method.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Develop Training Evaluation Model -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Develop Training Evaluation Model">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Develop Training Evaluation Model</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Develop Training Evaluation Model business activity generate the appraisal and rating structure to support the training plan.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Design Training Facility -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Design Training Facility">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Design Training Facility</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Design Training Facility business activity defines the specification required to support a training Plan.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Develop Training Plan -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Develop Training Plan">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Develop Training Plan</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Develop Training Plan business activity generate the detailed schedule and sequence of training activities that support achieving the training program.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Acquire Training Capability -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Acquire Training Capability">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Acquire Training Capability</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Acquire Training Capability business activity establishes and makes ready the capability required to support a training plan.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Schedule Training Program -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Schedule Training Program">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Schedule Training Program</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Acquire Training Capability business activity establishes and makes ready the capability required to support a training plan.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Implement Training Program -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Implement Training Program">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Implement Training Program</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Implement Training Program business activity executes training plans altogether to achieve the goals of a training program.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Select Training Method -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Select Training Method">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Select Training Method</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Select Training Method business activity makes a choice of the method of training to be used in a training program. Select Training Method  is responsible for guiding selection of the most appropriate training method(s). It takes input from the training assessment activity based on requirements identified between needs and gaps, and recommendations made during the Needs Analysis or training design activities.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Administer Training Program -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Administer Training Program">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Administer Training Program</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Administer Training Program business activity manages the responsibility for the implementation of the training program. Administer Training Program is responsible for the coordination of trainers with training capability and facility. It administers the recordkeeping that tracks training capability, training facility, training participation progress, as well as administrating and budgeting tasks associated with training programs.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Evaluate Training Outcome -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Evaluate Training Outcome">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Evaluate Training Outcome</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Evaluate Training Outcome business activity assesses results of training program on participants.  Evaluate Training Outcome provides feedback to help identify if training capability and facility achieved intended outcomes. It also helps to make decisions about future training capabilities and facilities.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Monitor Training -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Monitor Training">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Monitor Training</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Monitor Training business activity observes and tracks the enterprises training plans and programs. 
 Monitor Training business activity allows the enterprise to maintain control of the training processes, while ensuring proactive adaptive response to the business.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Evaluate Training Program -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Evaluate Training Program">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Evaluate Training Program</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Evaluate Training Program business activity assess the enterprises training program support its business goals.  Evaluate Training Program is the systematic process of collecting information and using that information to improve the enterprises training. Evaluate Training provides feedback to help identify if training programs achieve desired outcomes, and help make decisions about future training programs.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Manage Capital Investment -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Manage Capital Investment">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Manage Capital Investment</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Manage Capital Investment business activity directs and controls corporate expenditure of money to fund the enterprises long-term growth. 

Manage Capital Investment can facilitate enterprises acquisition of permanent fixed assets such as real estate and equipment, or provide diversification leveraging Manage Capital Investment business activity. This includes diversification strategies like replacements and modernization.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Manage Capital Financing -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Manage Capital Financing">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Manage Capital Financing</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Manage Capital Financing business activity directs and controls the methods the corporate business uses to raise money. 

Manage Capital Financing covers tasks that manage debt financing (i.e. borrowing money to pay for business operations) an equity financing (i.e. selling ownership stake in the enterprise).</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Manage Capital Structure -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Manage Capital Structure">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Manage Capital Structure</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Manage Capital Structure business activity directs and controls how the enterprise is financing its operations.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Manage Capital Budgeting -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Manage Capital Budgeting">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Manage Capital Budgeting</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Manage Capital Budgeting business activity directs and controls the evaluation of prospective investment. 

Manage Capital Budgeting helps to map out the cash outlays and cash inflows associated with an investment.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Manage Liquidity -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Manage Liquidity">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Manage Liquidity</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Manage Liquidity business activity directs and controls corporate visibility into the enterprise cash position. 

Manage Liquidity can be long-term, but for short-term it enables the enterprise to improve decision-making. Visibility into a firm's cash and liquidity position allows corporate treasurers to analyze surplus funds to make better investment and borrowing decisions.

This business activity handles tasks make decisions around working capital and operating cashflows (current assets and current liabilities) in order to avoid disrupting the enterprises business operations. These activities can extend to getting additional credit lines or activating liquidity backups.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Manage Managerial Accounting -->

<owl:Class rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Manage Managerial Accounting">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/ProcessModel_v1#Process"/>
<rdf:label>Manage Managerial Accounting</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Manage Managerial Accounting business activity directs, analyzes and communicates financial data to corporate managers who use the information to make business decisions.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>


	
	
</rdf:RDF>



